DESCRIPTION:Discover the beauty of\nNajeonchilgi\n\, the traditional Korea
 n art of mother-of-pearl inlay. In this hands-on workshop\, participants w
 ill explore simplified traditional techniques using colorful mother-of-pea
 rl pieces to create and decorate their own unique keepsake. No previous ex
 perience is required\, and all materials are provided.\nPlease note that r
 eserved seats are held until 5 minutes past the program start time. At 2:0
 5pm\, seats will become available on a first come\, first serve basis unti
 l capacity.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on t
 his form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libra
 ries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only b
 e used for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Quest
 ions about how the library handles your information can be directed to Ans
 werline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, 
 Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
