X-SOURCE-ID:meetup_the_history_of_parkdale
X-SOURCE:Meetup: History of Parkdale
UID:event_316868429@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20261010T053423Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261012T113000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261012T143000
SUMMARY:Fall Colour on the Historic Toronto Islands! 
DESCRIPTION:Toronto History Walks\n\\*\\***The Toronto History Walks Yearl
 y Pass is available. Get it now for $125.00 for 1 year of unlimited tours\
 , email**\n**torontohistorywalks@gmail.com**\n**for more information or fo
 r signing up!\\*\\***\n\n\\*\\* **Please note: Please e-transfer the ticke
 t price when booking your space for this tour! You can e-transfer to the f
 ollowing email at:**\n**torontohistorywalks@gmail.com**\n\nFor Fall colour
 \, it's hard to imagine a better place than the Toronto Islands. It's so m
 uch more than a small amusement park\, Chelsea Beach\, and walking and bik
 e trails. It's about growing up in Toronto. About the ten minute ride over
  on the ferry boat\, and the memories that have made Toronto a summertime 
 city. It's a stretch of land that is historic and fascinating\, both geolo
 gically and socially as well. And a history that brings together the stori
 es of Toronto from its founding.\n\nThe Gibraltar Point Lighthouse was con
 structed in 1809\, and is one of the oldest structures in Toronto. It is b
 est known for the ghost story of its murdered first keeper\, John Paul Rad
 emüller. But that's another story for another day.\n\nThe peninsula was p
 artially severed by a storm in 1852\, which created a sandbar that was dan
 gerously thin\, and the peninsula became an island permanently by a violen
 t storm that cut out the eastern channel\, two hotels on the island were a
 lso destroyed. The modern history of the Islands' begins here!\n\nThe Isla
 nds' have three main parts\, and all three have their historic elements\, 
 the most being the western most island named for the Hanlan family. A spec
 tacular hotel\, "The Ned Hanlan" was built and a regatta course dredged ou
 t of the western lagoon. An amusement park followed\, and an airport after
  that!\n\nIt was also a residential enclave with most of the homes appeari
 ng on Ward's and Centre Islands. By the 1950s these residential areas star
 ted to disappear\, as the idea of increasing city parkland took shape.\n\n
 **Take a quick peek at my introduction video which follows at** https://yo
 utu.be/hkVHx5Ol9qI\n\nThe tour begins and ends at the Jack Layton Ferry Te
 rminal at the foot of Bay Street. We will meet **inside** the gates! And w
 e will head over as a group\, so tickets must be bought before! Please mee
 t 10 minutes before the meetup time!\n\nThis tour has a ticket price of $1
 5.00 per person!\n\n\\*\\* **Please note: Please e-transfer the ticket pri
 ce when booking your space for this tour! You can e-transfer to the follow
 ing email at:**\n**torontohistorywalks@gmail.com**
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/the-history-of-parkdale/events/316868
 429/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20261006T134225Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20261006T134225Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
