X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_adults
SUMMARY:Connect 4: A Conversation Workshop with GenWell
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261013T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261013T190000
UID:6ac69b53295b3b0033cadd08@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Connect4 Workshop with GenWell\nA playful\, no-pressure challe
 nge that turns strangers into new connections — one quick conversation a
 t a time. This lighthearted pre-show activity invites you to join our “s
 ocial” experiment and step out of your comfort zone into a few unexpecte
 d conversations. Inspired by our evening's speakers\, Dr. Nick Epley and D
 r. Gillian Sandstrom\, and in partnership with GenWell\, Canada's Human Co
 nnection Movement\, we're turning the simple act of talking to someone new
  into a game — equal parts curiosity\, fun\, and connection. No scripts\
 , no pressure — just a chance to discover how easy (and rewarding) it ca
 n be to connect with people you don't already know.\nYou'll leave with a f
 ew new acquaintances\, a fresh take on why talking to "strangers" isn’t 
 strange\, and a tool or two to keep connection going long after you leave 
 the library.\nInsights from this interactive workshop will be shared in\nS
 ay Hello to Connecting featuring Nick Epley and Gillian Sandstrom\n\, whic
 h follows at 7pm in the Appel Salon.\nYou can\nregister for that event her
 e\n.\nAbout this event's guests:\nGenWell\nis a Canadian charity on a miss
 ion to improve the nation's social health by inspiring more meaningful hum
 an connection. Through research\, storytelling\, workshops\, and hands-on 
 initiatives\, they help people rebuild the everyday habits — big and sma
 ll — that reduce feelings of loneliness\, disconnection\, and isolation.
 \n****\nThis interactive workshop is followed by\nHello to Connecting ft. 
 Nicholas Epley and Gillian Sandstorm\n\, which starts at 7pm in the Appel 
 Salon.\nYou can register for that event\nhere\n\, but please note if you w
 ish to attend the pre-event workshop you need to register separately\non t
 his page\n.\n***\nMake the most of your\nConnect IRL\nexperience by coming
  before or staying after the\nfeatured event\n. Grab a drink or snack at t
 he bar. Sign up for the workshop or try out one of the engagement activiti
 es available\, including this event's\nConversation Station: The\nBus Stop
  Challenge\n\, where you can take a moment or two to connect with a strang
 er in the most ordinary of small-talk settings.\nThe Bus Stop Challenge |\
 n5:30 – 7:00 pm & 8:00 – 9:00 pm\nConnect IRL\nis not your average ser
 ies of events\, workshops and activities\, but a real chance to connect wi
 th other Torontonians in meaningful and sometimes unexpected ways. Through
  conversation stations meant to spark one-on-one conversations\, or hands-
 on engagement activities and workshops before the featured event\, partici
 pants can explore the value of connection and community.\n***\nPLAN YOUR V
 ISIT:\nLocation:\nBram and Bluma Appel Salon\, Toronto Reference Library (
 789 Yonge Street)\, 2nd floor\nTime:\nDoors open 5:15pm\, Event starts at 
 approximately 5:30pm.\nTickets:\nFree registration required.\nTicket polic
 y:\nWe oversell these events to ensure that the greatest number of people 
 have an opportunity to attend. Tickets guaranteed until 5:45pm or until ca
 pacity is reached. Seating first come\, first served.\nBar\n: Beer/wine av
 ailable for purchase (debit/credit only).\nAccessibility:\nTPL is committe
 d to accessibility. If you are Deaf or have a disability and would like to
  request accommodation for this event\, please contact accessibleservices@
 tpl.ca or 416-393-7099 at least three weeks prior to the event.\n***\nInfo
 rmation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is colle
 cted by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sectio
 ns 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event 
 and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Registrants may be con
 tacted to fill out a brief survey following the program. Questions about h
 ow the library handles your information can be directed to Answerline staf
 f at answerline@tpl.ca\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 
 2G8.
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, Bram and Bluma Appel Salon\, Toronto 
 Reference Library (789 Yonge Street)\, 2nd floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ac69b53295b3b0033cadd08
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
