X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Civic Tech Toronto": "https://guild.host/events/civic-meetup-564-a-datadriven-w2fxru"}
X-SOURCE-ID:guildhost_civic_tech
SUMMARY:Civic Meetup #564: A Data-Driven Approach to Toronto's Electoral G
 eography
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261013T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261013T210000
UID:abce6f82a43b485ffeeb262649402740@guild.host
DESCRIPTION:Venue confirmed: Health Sciences Building (University of Toron
 to)\, Room 108\, 155 College St. Please note: this is not Myhal Centre as 
 originally listed.&#x20\;\n\nTopic: A Data-Driven Approach to Toronto's El
 ectoral Geography\n\nWith colleagues\, Zach Taylor built for research purp
 oses fine-grained maps of historical election results in Toronto and other
  cities. He will discuss how they built the maps\, what they have used the
 m for\, and how spatial data like this could be used in the future.\n\nSpe
 aker: Zack Taylor (he/him) joining via Zoom\n\nZack Taylor is a professor 
 of Political Science and Geography at the University of Western Ontario wh
 ere he specializes in urban politics\, local governance\, and political ge
 ography.\n\nAgenda:\n\n7:00-7:20 Welcome and Introductions\n\n7:20-7:50 Pr
 esentation and Q\\&A/discussion\n\n7:50-9:00 Breakout groups\n\n‎\n\nCod
 e of Conduct: https://civictech.ca/about-us\n\n‎\n\nCheck in with us on 
 the Civic Tech Toronto Slack: https://link.civictech.ca/chat\n\n‎\n\nAbo
 ut Us:\n\nOur weekly civic meetups bring together Torontonians (designers\
 , coders\, urban planners\, government staff\, mappers\, policy-makers\, s
 tudents\, communications strategists\, community organizers\, and more) wh
 o share an interest in making Toronto more responsive\, prosperous\, susta
 inable\, and equitable through design\, tech\, and data.\n\nCome and be pa
 rt of it!\n\nFor more info: https://civictech.ca\n\n\\--\n\nSuggest a Spea
 ker:&#x20\;\n\nInterested in speaking at a future event\, or know someone 
 who'd be a great speaker? We'd love to hear from you: https://link.civicte
 ch.ca/speaker-suggestions\n\nSuggest a Venue:&#x20\;\n\nHave a space that 
 could host up to 80 civic-minded folks for an evening? Consider recommendi
 ng your venue: https://link.civictech.ca/venue-suggestions\n
LOCATION:Online: https://link.civictech.ca/zoom / Health Sciences Building
URL:https://guild.host/events/civic-meetup-564-a-datadriven-w2fxru
X-SOURCE:Civic Tech Toronto
END:VEVENT
