BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Older Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ab18ba1ca248a00291766e5"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_older_adults
SUMMARY:A Little More Social with Author Nicholas Epley
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261014T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261014T111500
UID:6ab18ba1ca248a00291766e5@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:We are social beings by nature and are equipped to connect wit
 h others. Yet in today's increasingly disconnected world\, many people exp
 erience loneliness or isolation. As we age\, we may also face new and uniq
 ue barriers to forming and maintaining meaningful connections.\nJoin autho
 r and psychologist\nNicholas Epley\nwho will explore why people may choose
  to be less social and the impact this can have on our health and well-bei
 ng. He will share practical strategies and simple actions that can help ol
 der adults and seniors strengthen social connections and become a little m
 ore social. Participants can also take part in a short interactive worksho
 p led by Nicholas. Light refreshments will be provided.\nDrop in or regist
 er in advance to receive a reminder or drop-in on the day.\nA Little More 
 Social
LOCATION:Lillian H. Smith
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ab18ba1ca248a00291766e5
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
