 ms),Graduate Program in Civil Engineering,Graduate Program in Electrical E
 ngineering &amp\; Computer Science,Graduate Program in Mechanical Engineer
 ing
CLASS:PUBLIC
CREATED:20260929
DESCRIPTION:Are you thinking of pursuing your graduate education in Sustai
 nable Energy Systems ( https://yorku.zoom.us/meeting/register/Hd7g515vT2iw
 kKMHAv1XIQ )? We invite you to attend our program session. Registration is
  required ( https://yorku.zoom.us/meeting/register/Hd7g515vT2iwkKMHAv1XIQ 
 )!\nThe Master of Engineering (MEng) in Sustainable Energy Systems is a co
 urse-based graduate degree offered through the Department of Mechanical En
 gineering at York University’s Lassonde School of Engineering. It’s de
 signed for people who want to enter or advance within the sustainable ener
 gy sector\, with a strong focus on career outcomes\, applied learning\, an
 d professional growth. Rather than a research thesis\, this program emphas
 izes advanced coursework\, real-world applications\, and leadership develo
 pment—so you graduate ready to contribute at a higher level. Please note
 : this session will cover all programs available in the Lassonde School of
  Engineering.\nLearn more about our graduate programs at futurestudents.yo
 rku.ca/graduate/programs  ( http://futurestudents.yorku.ca/graduate/progra
 ms )\nStill have questions? Contact us at fgsapply@yorku.ca ( mailto:fgs
 apply@yorku.ca ).\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20260929
LOCATION:(URL will be provided in the email confirmation)
ORGANIZER;CN="Faculty of Graduate Studies":MAILTO:fgsinfo@yorku.ca
PRIORITY:5
TRANSP:OPAQUE
