X-SOURCE-ID:events
SUMMARY:Scholars’ Hub | Beyond Tokenism: Building meaningful inclusion f
 or women\, girls\, and gender-diverse youth in sports
DTSTART:20261014T160000Z
DTEND:20261014T170000Z
DTSTAMP:20260928T195600Z
UID:MEC-38db417df0ff3f93630307983ebb21f8@events.yorku.ca
RECURRENCE-ID:20261014T160000Z
SEQUENCE:11
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://events.yorku.ca/wp-content/uploads/2026/0
 9/scholarsHub_CRMbanner_2026update__1_.png
CATEGORIES:Advancement/Alumni
CLASS:PUBLIC
CREATED:20260928
DESCRIPTION:Speaker: Lyndsay Hayhurst\, Research Chair and Associate Profe
 ssor\, School of Kinesiology and Health Science\, Faculty of Health\nIn th
 is session\, we’ll explore the idea that sport is a human right and why 
 inclusion is essential to making that right a reality. Community-based spo
 rt-for-development programs can create more welcoming\, supportive\, and m
 eaningful opportunities for gender-diverse youth to participate in sport.
  Attendees will gain a practical framework for thinking about inclusion\,
  not as an add-on to sport\, but as essential to its purpose. \nNote: Thi
 s event has been postponed.\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20261009
ORGANIZER;CN="Alumni Engagement":MAILTO:alumnievents@yorku.ca
PRIORITY:5
TRANSP:OPAQUE
