SUMMARY:Vibe Coding: Make Your Own Interactive Story with AI
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261014T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261014T200000
UID:6a9b4e24aafa61002961b09b@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:What if you could write a story where the reader chooses what 
 happens\, like a branching adventure\, a mystery\, or a game\, and have AI
  build it with you?\nIn this class\, you'll learn "vibe-coding" with our I
 nnovator-in-Residence\,\nRyan Kelln\n: using an AI coding assistant to bui
 ld your own interactive story or simple game. You'll design the branches\,
  describe the rules in plain language\, test for the tricky edge cases (wh
 at if the player picks the weird option?)\, and end up with a single file 
 you can share with anyone. Just a story you want to tell. This is the play
 ful sibling of the practical vibe-coding workshop.\nPrerequisites: Mouse\
 , keyboarding and internet skills. Computers are provided. No coding exp
 erience required. If you wish to save your work from this hands-on progra
 m\, please bring your own USB stick.\nRegistration is required and will st
 art September 9\, 2026 at 9:00 AM.\nNote: Your spot will not be guaranteed
  after 5 minutes of the start of the program.\nAfter this time\, remaining
  seats will be filled on a first come\, first serve basis until capacity i
 s reached.\nAbout the AI Tools Used in This Program\nThis program includes
  activities that use agentic AI tools (listed below) on library laptops.\n
 You do not need to create your own account for this program.\nParticipants
  are encouraged to follow the Resident’s guidance throughout sessions\, 
 which include best practices on using AI.\nWe encourage you to review the 
 privacy statements of each tool prior to attending this program:\nClaude C
 ode\nLearn more about the tool\nReview privacy policy\nGoogle Antigravity\
 nLearn more about the tool\nReview privacy policy\nGoogle AI Studio\nLearn
  more about the tool\nReview privacy policy\nInformation Collection Notice
 :\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Publi
 c Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20
 (d). The information will only be used for event and program registration\
 , delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your in
 formation can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 41
 6-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, 2nd Floor eLearning Lab
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a9b4e24aafa61002961b09b
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
