SUMMARY:*FULL -Human Connection 101 Workshop Series for Seniors
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261015T133000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261015T150000
UID:6ac407bf686221156abb5674@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Human connection has a profound impact on our health and happi
 ness\, especially in our increasingly disconnected world. Join GenWell in 
 an interactive 5-week (Oct 1\, 8\, 15\, 22 & 29) program series to learn p
 ractical ways to enhance social health\, understand the adverse effects of
  loneliness\, and discover the benefits of building more meaningful connec
 tions. Receive a free social health workbook\, spend time with other parti
 cipants after the workshops\, and enjoy some light refreshments provided.\
 nAbout GenWell: Founded in 2016\, GenWell is a registered charity whose mi
 ssion is to make the world a happier and healthier place by educating\, em
 powering\, and catalyzing forty million Canadians about the importance of 
 their social health.\nRegistration full.
LOCATION:Fairview\, Room 201
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ac407bf686221156abb5674
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
