SUMMARY:Who decides what matters – Us or the model?
DTSTART:20261015T153000Z
DTEND:20261015T163000Z
DTSTAMP:20261008T141900Z
UID:MEC-d7df9a10a3bb2c94ef6f35d90282702f@events.yorku.ca
RECURRENCE-ID:20261015T153000Z
SEQUENCE:2
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://events.yorku.ca/wp-content/uploads/2026/
 10/IEFLL-Research-Presentation-Clara-Oct-15-scaled.jpg
CATEGORIES:Faculty of Environmental &amp\; Urban Change,Sustainability
CLASS:PUBLIC
CREATED:20261008
DESCRIPTION:This event will explore the paradigmatic commitments in the mo
 delling of systemic transformation.\n\n\n\n\n\nClara Barbara Stephan Klink
 enberg\, a Master’s student at the University of Iceland\, will present 
 her thesis research investigating how various computational modelling para
 digms differ in their capacity to represent systemic transformation\, whic
 h she then applied to existing sustainability transformation models.\n\nTh
 is presentation and Clara’s research are part of the International Ecolo
 gical Footprint Learning Lab\, a research partnership based at York Univer
 sity through the Ecological Footprint Initiative.\n\n\n\nThis virtual even
 t is hosted on Zoom\, register here: Meeting Registration – Zoom ( https
 ://yorku.zoom.us/meeting/register/iAHfqpS4Qlu277VDKGHtBQ#/registration )\n
 \n\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20261008
PRIORITY:5
TRANSP:OPAQUE
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/who-decides-what-matters-us-or-the-mode
 l/
X-SOURCE:York University
