SUMMARY:In Conversation with Jane Lytvynenko
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261015T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261015T200000
UID:6aac2d36a5dbde002aa54c84@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a conversation with Jane Lytvynenko\, one of the l
 eading voices on misinformation\, political manipulation\, and the future 
 of democracy. In an interview-style discussion\, Wency Leung (The Local) w
 ill explore Lytvynenko's research and insights on how misinformation is cr
 eated and spread\, the\nJane Lytvynenko\ninfluence of foreign actors\, and
  the role social media plays in shaping public understanding. Together\, t
 hey'll discuss what journalists\, civil society organizations\, and everyd
 ay people can do to strengthen a healthy information ecosystem and support
  democratic resilience.\nFeaturing:\nJane Lytvynenko is a senior technolog
 y reporter at NBC News\, where she covers technology and conflict. Previou
 sly\, she covered the war in Ukraine for The Wall Street Journal. She liv
 es in New York.\nWency Leung is a senior reporter for\nThe Local\nmagazine
 \, covering education\, health\, and other social issues in the Greater To
 ronto Area.\nToronto's municipal election takes place on October 26\, 2026
 . Check out the\nKnowYourVote.TO\nwebsite and the\nCelebrate Democracy\np
 age to learn more about the upcoming election\, access important voter res
 ources\, and discover more activities and interactive library programs for
  all ages happening at a branch near you.\nThis initiative is made possibl
 e by donations to the Toronto Public Library Foundation and is generously 
 supported by the McConnell Foundation\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe
  personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Libr
 ary under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). T
 he information will only be used for event and program registration\, deli
 very and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your informat
 ion can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-
 5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aac2d36a5dbde002aa54c84
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Preschool
END:VEVENT
