SUMMARY:After School Story and Craft: Mindfulness
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261016T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261016T164500
UID:6aad7c3b3dd190003e72eb61@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Children age 3-12 are invited to come hear the beautiful story
 \,\nThe Three Questions\n\, by Jon Muth. After the story\, each child can 
 make a set of tiny worry dolls to take home. Worry dolls are tiny handmade
  dolls used in the Guatemalan tradition. Children can whisper their worry 
 to a doll at bedtime and then place the doll under their pillow. The doll
  will carry the worry away while the child sleeps so the child can awake w
 ith a peaceful mind.\nFrom the publisher: "Jon J Muth combined his studies
  of Zen with his love for Tolstoy to create this profound\, yet simple boo
 k about compassion and living in the moment."\nInformation Collection Noti
 ce:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Pub
 lic Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 
 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program registratio
 n\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your 
 information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 
 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Gerrard/Ashdale\, 2nd Floor Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aad7c3b3dd190003e72eb61
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Preschool
END:VEVENT
