X-SOURCE-ID:a_different_booklist
SUMMARY:Black & Caribbean Book Affair 2026
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261016T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261016T200000
UID:bm-6512620261016@adifferentbooklist.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://cdn1.bookmanager.com/i/1188585/FB_IMG_17
 91140196635.jpg?cb=1791148698
DESCRIPTION:📚Three days of books and ideas that reflect who we are!\n\n
 The Black & Caribbean Book Affair 2026 returns to Blackhurst CC from Oct 1
 5–17th under the theme Seeing Ourselves: The Next Chapter.\n🔹Oct 15 |
  6–8 PM\nDr. Carl James discusses Seeing Ourselves: Exploring Race\, Eth
 nicity & Culture\, 5th ed.\, with educators M. Proudfoot and A. Dualeh.\n
 🔹Oct 16 | 6–8 PM\nRamie Veerappan joins S. Whiting for a conversation
  about Ramie’s Dance of Resilience: Apartheid and Beyond\, by Romila Log
 arahjah-Jeevithan.\n🔹Oct 17 | 9–10 AM on Zoom: Gelien Matthews and Rh
 oma Spencer discuss Calypso Rose\, who broke through the male-dominated ca
 lypso world.\n11 AM–1 PM: A Parade of Children’s Books with Heather Be
 aumont\, Delano Brown and host Yolanda Marshall.\n4:30–6:30 PM: Didier L
 eclair launches The African Prince\, the Translator\, and the Nazi in conv
 ersation with Canute Lawrence.\nJoin us as Black & Caribbean stories take 
 centre stage!📚
LOCATION:BLACKHURST CULTURAL CENTRE
URL:https://adifferentbooklist.com/events
X-SOURCE:A Different Booklist
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events": "https://events.yorku.ca/events/co-op-information-session-3/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events
SUMMARY:Co-op Information Session
DTSTART:20261016T180000Z
DTEND:20261016T190000Z
DTSTAMP:20261002T131000Z
UID:MEC-1b52316d70bb30edd173db4f2805c856@events.yorku.ca
RECURRENCE-ID:20261016T180000Z
SEQUENCE:3
CATEGORIES:Co-op &amp\; Career Centre,Co-op Information Session,Co-op Mand
 atory Sessions (CCC),Information Sessions (CCC)
CLASS:PUBLIC
CREATED:20261002
DESCRIPTION:\nYork University Co-op Information Session (live webinar)\nLo
 cation: Online – Link:  https://yorku.zoom.us/my/askcoop\nDate: Octobe
 r 16\, 2026\nTime: 2:00pm-3:30pm\nThe York University Co-op Program provi
 des students with opportunities for paid\, hands-on learning and valuable 
 industry experience. We encourage you to visit the Co-operative Education 
 website to review program details and confirm that you meet the academic r
 equirements.\nDuring this session\, you will learn about:\n\nThe co-op adv
 antage\nEligibility requirements\nProgram fees\nThe registration process\n
 General Q&A with a Co-op Coordinator\n\nTarget Audience:\nThese sessions a
 re for York University students intending to begin their first co-op work 
 term in Summer 2027. Before registering\, please self-assess your eligibi
 lity for the program ( https://www.yorku.ca/career-ready/work-opportunitie
 s/co-op/eligibility/ ).\nSessions are available in three formats to suppor
 t your schedule and learning preferences:\n\nIn-person\nLive webinar (Zoom
 )\nSelf-paced online modules through the Co-op Preparatory Course (eClass)
 \n\n\nLive Session vs. Self-Paced Modules: What’s the Difference?\nBased
  on student feedback\, we now offer flexible options to complete the requi
 red sessions. Each format has unique benefits:\n\nLive sessions (in-person
  or webinar): Opportunity to ask questions and interact directly with a C
 o-op Coordinator.\nSelf-paced eClass modules: Complete the content at a t
 ime that is most convenient for you.\n\n\nImportant Reminders:\n\nRequired
  sessions must be completed for your application to be reviewed.\nAlready 
 attended a mandatory session within the last 12 months? You do not need to
  attend again.\nAlready admitted to Co-op? You are not required to complet
 e the mandatory sessions or re-apply.\nIf you have an eligible work term f
 or Summer 2027: Log in to the co-op portal and accept the terms and condit
 ions when prompted.\n\nWe look forward to your participation!\nHaving trou
 ble logging in? \nPlease make sure you’re using your PPY York U login. 
 When you select SSO (Single Sign-On)\, you should be prompted to sign in w
 ith your PPY credentials. If you use a different login\, you may not be ab
 le to access the system.\nRegister Here [icon name=”chevron-right” cla
 ss=”small pl-2″]\n \nAccessibility\nIf you require accommodations\, p
 lease contact askcoop@yorku.ca\, and a member of our team will follow up 
 with you.\nCode of Conduct\nBefore attending\, please review the Code of 
 Rights and Responsibilities from the York University Office of Student Co
 mmunity Relations to help ensure a respectful and positive experience for 
 all participants.\nGuests who exhibit behaviour that violates this code ma
 y be removed from the event. If you experience behaviour that does not ali
 gn with these expectations\, please contact our team at askcoop@yorku.ca.
 \n \n
LAST-MODIFIED:20261006
PRIORITY:5
TRANSP:OPAQUE
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/co-op-information-session-3/
X-SOURCE:York University
END:VEVENT
