DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261017T070000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261017T180000
SUMMARY:Wilder Series: The Even Wilder Loop
DESCRIPTION:Wilderness Union Toronto - Outdoor Adventure and Hiking Club\n
 **Please note the only way to register for this adventure is on [our websi
 te.](https://www.wildernessunion.com/adventures/wilder-loop-fall-26)**\n**
 We're heading somewhere new\, and it's wilder than anything else in the se
 ries.**\nThis is the first time WU is running the Even Wilder Loop\, and i
 t's the next step up in our Wilder Series\, our lineup for those chasing b
 igger days out. The name isn't subtle. This is a remote\, rugged backcount
 ry in a less visited part of the park\, and you'll feel it from the first 
 kilometre.\nThe trail climbs and drops hard in places\, with some scramble
 s along the way where you'll need your hands as well as your feet. Between
  the climbs\, it opens onto barrens and meadows\, and you'll see plenty of
  beaver dams along the way.\nPartway through\, the river crossing takes us
  through some rapids.\nIt's only 8.5 km\, but it's some of the wildest 8.5
  km we run.\n***Secret Location***\nThis is one of Wilderness Union's 'sec
 ret' hikes. As a group\, we visit some truly special spots that are undisc
 overed by the wider world. We like to keep them pristine and only share th
 em among our members - we ask that you do the same! We reveal the location
  to registered members in the days before the trip.\n**Accessibility**\nWi
 lderness Union is committed to making our adventures as accessible as poss
 ible. If you wish to make an accommodation request relating to a disabilit
 y or provide feedback\, please do so by sending an email to info@wildernes
 sunion.com\n**Highlights**\n**The Rapids Crossing:** The most memorable st
 retch of the day. You will get wet!\n**Wildlife Spotting:** Bears\, moose\
 , beavers and loons are just some of the creatures that call this area hom
 e. You'll have a chance to spot some from a safe distance for a magical en
 counter.\n**A WU First:** Nobody in the crew has done this loop with us be
 fore. You'll be part of the first group on it.\n**Itinerary**\n**07:00** \
 \- Shuttle leaves from near Keele station\n**10:00 - 15:00** \\- Hike loop
  at secret location\n**15:00** \\- Anticipated return to cars\n**18:00** \
 \- Anticipated return to Toronto\n**Event cost: $66+HST. $50+HST optional 
 transport also available. Please register [here.](https://www.wildernessun
 ion.com/adventures/wilder-loop-fall-26)**\n**About Wilderness Union**\nWil
 derness Union is deliberate about building an outdoors community that conn
 ects you to the life-changing magic of the outdoors and helps you find you
 r people.\nMembers range from 20-40 years old. The group is a mix of GTA l
 ocals and newcomers to Toronto from within Canada and abroad.\nAttendance 
 numbers on Meetup don't reflect our actual event attendance - we typically
  have 15-20 community members at each event. Large enough that there's som
 eone new to meet but small enough that it's not overwhelming!\n***Learn mo
 re at our website [www.wildernessunion.com](https://www.wildernessunion.co
 m/)***
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/wildernessunion/events/316616155/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260918T205104Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260918T205104Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
