SUMMARY:🚐 Doors Open Niagara-on-the-Lake Road Trip!  Saturday\, October
  17
DESCRIPTION:Toronto Movies & Social Group - Celebrating 14 Years!\n**🚐 
 Doors Open Niagara-on-the-Lake Road Trip!**\n**Saturday\, October 17**\n\n
 Let’s hit the road for another Doors Open adventure! We’ll be heading 
 to beautiful **Doors Open Niagara-on-the-Lake** to explore historic buildi
 ngs\, cultural sites\, and hidden spaces that are rarely open to the publi
 c.\nNick has been a **Doors Open Toronto volunteer for over two decades**\
 , and he always enjoys checking out Doors Open events in other cities. Nia
 gara-on-the-Lake is known for its incredible heritage architecture\, charm
 ing streets\, and fascinating history—making it a perfect destination fo
 r a Doors Open day trip.\n\n***\n\n### 🏛️ What is Doors Open?\n\nIf y
 ou’ve never attended before\, **Doors Open** is a free architectural and
  cultural event held in communities across Ontario. For one special weeken
 d\, cities open the doors to historic buildings\, cultural institutions\, 
 churches\, theatres\, and other interesting spaces—many of which are nor
 mally closed to the public.\nVisitors can explore at their own pace\, lear
 n about local history\, and sometimes go behind the scenes with guided tou
 rs or special access.\n\nLearn more about the event here:\n👉 [https://w
 ww.doorsopenontario.on.ca/pages/events/niagara-on-the-lake](https://www.do
 orsopenontario.on.ca/pages/events/niagara-on-the-lake)\n\n***\n\n### 🗓
 ️ The Plan\n\n* **Departure:** 8:00 AM from just outside **Christie Stat
 ion**\n* **Transportation:** Rental minivan or SUV\n* **Destination:** **N
 iagara-on-the-Lake**\n* Spend the day exploring **Doors Open sites around 
 town**\n* Time permitting we may be able to visit Niagara Falls after for 
 a few photos/sightseeing\n* **Return to Toronto:** Around **6:00 PM**\, de
 pending on traffic\n\nYou’re welcome to explore with the group or wander
  off to check out sites that interest you most. The day will be relaxed an
 d flexible.\n\n***\n\n### 🍽️ Food & Drink\n\nYou are responsible for 
 **your own food and drink purchases** throughout the day.\n\n***\n\n### 
 💰 Cost\n\n**$60 round-trip**\nThis covers:\n\n* Car rental\n* Insurance
 \n* Fuel\n\nTo secure your spot\, **all participants must e-transfer $60 t
 o:**\n📧 **[nicolasbello@yahoo.com](mailto:nicolasbello@yahoo.com)**\nSp
 ots are limited based on vehicle capacity\, so please RSVP only if you’r
 e able to commit.\n\n***\n\n### 🌦️ Weather Note\n\nThis event **runs 
 rain or shine**\, so please **dress appropriately for the weather**. The g
 ood news is that we’ll be **inside most of the time**\, but there will s
 till be some walking between locations.\n\n***\n\n### 🎒 What to Bring\n
 \n* Comfortable walking shoes\n* Curiosity & good vibes\n* A little patien
 ce for traffic (it’s part of the road-trip charm!)\n\nJoin us for a fun 
 architectural adventure and a chance to explore one of Ontario’s most hi
 storic towns. 🚐🏛️
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/toronto-movies-and-social-group/event
 s/313710666/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260309T124647Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260309T124647Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Torontobotanicalgarden": "https://torontobotanicalgarden.ca/event/birding-with-beni-fall-birding-3/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:torontobotanicalgarden
X-SOURCE:Toronto Botanical Garden
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261017T080000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261017T100000
DTSTAMP:20261010T013517
CREATED:20260728T145502Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260911T195106Z
UID:10002007-1792224000-1792231200@torontobotanicalgarden.ca
SUMMARY:SOLD OUT: Birding with Beni: Fall Birding
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a fall birding nature walk!\nFall migration is well underway! Join TBG Horticulturist and avid birder Sasan Beni for an engaging walk through the gardens and Wilket Creek Ravine\, as you seek out the wildlife that call this place home. Learn how to identify the many different species passing through and how you can help them in their journey.\n \nBring your binoculars for a better view (we will have extras on hand) and a mug/thermos for a warm beverage and post-birding chat.\n \nAs with any wildlife tour\, the spotting of birds and other wildlife is not guaranteed and is not within the control of the tour guide. Please be patient and considerate. The tour will not be rescheduled due to a lack of bird sightings. The tour will only be rescheduled due to inclement weather.\n \nMeet at the TBG main entrance\, just outside the George and Kathy Dembroski Centre for Horticulture.\n \nSaturday\, October 17\, 8 to 10 a.m.\nPublic $22\, Members $20 (plus applicable taxes and fees).\n \nAbout Sasan Beni\nSasan Beni is a writer turned horticulturist. He graduated with a diploma in Environmental Landscape Management from Seneca College in King City\, worked for the Toronto Zoo as a seasonal gardener\, and joined TBG in 2020 as a seasonal Horticulturalist. His home is a revolving door of tropical plants. Beni is also passionate about birdwatching and wildlife photography. In the last three years\, he has led many guided birdwatching walks around Toronto and has written several articles for Trellis magazine illustrated with his nature photographs.\n \nJoin Toronto Botanical Garden\nJoin the Toronto Botanical Garden (TBG) as a member to get a discount on this program\, upcoming events and classes\, and free parking. A TBG membership helps you deepen your knowledge and connection to the natural world\, become a part of a dynamic community of plant people\, and be inspired! Become a member!\n \nAccessibility\nThe walk will be at a leisurely pace throughout\, following designated pathways and trails but sometimes covering uneven terrain and steep inclines. Dress appropriately for the weather and walk slowly. Wearing layers is recommended. Closed-toed shoes are required. We will begin promptly. \nNOTE: This program occurs rain or shine (save for cases of extreme weather); please dress appropriately for the weather.\n \nAdditional Program Information\n\n\n\nPlease review our Refund Policy and Terms of Agreement.\nFor more information on accessibility at the garden please review our Accessibility Features webpage. If you have any accessibility requirements during your program please email programsupport@torontobotanicalgarden.ca.\nTo learn more about the Toronto Botanical Garden and our programs\, please review our list of Frequently Asked Questions.
URL:https://torontobotanicalgarden.ca/event/birding-with-beni-fall-birding-3/
LOCATION:Toronto Botanical Garden\, 777 Lawrence Ave E\, Toronto\, ON\, M3C 1P2\, Canada
CATEGORIES:Gardening
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://torontobotanicalgarden.ca/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/9834645e7e661edda07a98c5639a5e2a.jpg
END:VEVENT
