SUMMARY:Black & Caribbean Book Affair
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261017T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261017T183000
UID:bm-6512520261017@adifferentbooklist.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://cdn1.bookmanager.com/i/1188585/20261004_
 165806_0000_1_.png?cb=1791149198
DESCRIPTION:📚Three days of books and ideas that reflect who we are!\n\n
 The Black & Caribbean Book Affair 2026 returns to Blackhurst CC from Oct 1
 5–17th under the theme Seeing Ourselves: The Next Chapter.\n🔹Oct 15 |
  6–8 PM\nDr. Carl James discusses Seeing Ourselves: Exploring Race\, Eth
 nicity & Culture\, 5th ed.\, with educators M. Proudfoot and A. Dualeh.\n
 🔹Oct 16 | 6–8 PM\nRamie Veerappan joins Sandra Whiting for a conversa
 tion about Ramie’s Dance of Resilience: Apartheid and Beyond\, by Romila
  Logarahjah-Jeevithan.\n🔹Oct 17 | 9–10 AM on Zoom: Gelien Matthews an
 d Rhoma Spencer discuss Calypso Rose\, who broke through the male-dominate
 d calypso world.\n11 AM–1 PM: A Parade of Children’s Books with Heathe
 r Beaumont\, Delano Brown and host Yolanda Marshall.\n4:30–6:30 PM: Didi
 er Leclair launches The African Prince\, the Translator\, and the Nazi in 
 conversation with Canute Lawrence.\nJoin us as Black & Caribbean stories t
 ake centre stage!📚
LOCATION:Blackhurst Cultural Centre
URL:https://adifferentbooklist.com/events
X-SOURCE:A Different Booklist
END:VEVENT
