BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ab16547001a4a0e055af05e"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_adults
SUMMARY:Club de lecture de Brentwood
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261019T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261019T200000
UID:6ab16547001a4a0e055af05e@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Aimez-vous lire en français? Avez-vous envie de participer à
  des discussions autour des livres dans une ambiance conviviale et déten
 due?\nRejoignez notre club de lecture en français! Venez échanger vos po
 ints de vue\, analyser ce qui vous a marqué avec le regard d'autres lecte
 urs\, et faire de belles découvertes littéraires.\nOn se réunit le 19 o
 ctobre pour découvrir\n« Pis\, un jour\, il a fallu faire des lunchs\,
  » de\nBlaise Durivage.\nLe livre sera disponible en prêt à la bibliot
 hèque\nBrentwood\n\, au comptoir de prêt\, à partir du 21 septembre.\nS
 i vous voulez en savoir plus sur nos clubs de lectures\, veuillez nous env
 oyer un courriel à\nprogrammesenfrancais@tpl.ca\nVeuillez noter que ce pr
 ogramme s’adresse aux personnes francophones ainsi qu’à celles ayant 
 un niveau avancé en français. Il est nécessaire de pouvoir lire\, discu
 ter et critiquer un livre avec une aisance de communication en français.\
 nSi vous souhaitez pratiquer votre français mais que vous avez plutôt un
  niveau débutant ou intermédiaire\, nous vous encourageons à découvrir
  nos cercles de conversation.\nLe sous-titrage en direct ou automatique\, 
 l’interprétation en langue des signes\, les services d’intervenant\, 
 ou les services d’accompagnement sont disponibles sur demande. Veuillez 
 soumettre votre demande au moins deux semaines à l’avance à :\ntpl.ca/
 accessibility-events\n.
LOCATION:Brentwood
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ab16547001a4a0e055af05e
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a85b648f564ef0d72c0eb0a"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_adults
SUMMARY:David Treuer: The Savage Mind
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261019T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261019T200000
UID:6a85b648f564ef0d72c0eb0a@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:New York Times bestselling author David Treuer shares his grou
 ndbreaking\, intimate reckoning with the history of North America.\nThe Sa
 vage Mind is a seamless blend of memoir\, history and reportage\, in which
  Treuer leverages his unique dual perspective as the son of a Holocaust su
 rvivor and the first American Indigenous woman judge in the United States 
 to offer an examination of the distinct nature of North American violence.
 \nIn contrast to the frontier thesis of American history\, Treuer contends
  that frontier violence cannot be defined as an external force\, but that 
 it has actually entered the culture and taken root in our very selves.\nBy
  reckoning with these histories\, the book confronts our complicity in eit
 her normalizing violence\, or blaming it on outside sources\, instead of s
 eeing its recurring patterns and contending with its significance.\nDavid 
 Treuer speaks with journalist and author Tanya Talaga about The Savage Min
 d and shares why he chooses to embrace an ultimately hopefully view of the
  continent.\nQ&A and book signing to follow. Books available for purchase.
 \nAbout this event’s guests:\nDavid Treuer\nTanya Talaga\nRead more:\nSa
 vage Mind : An Indigenous Legacy\nThe Heartbeat of Wounded Knee\nThe Knowi
 ng\nSeven Fallen Feathers\n***\nPLAN YOUR VISIT:\nLocation:\nBram and Blum
 a Appel Salon\, Toronto Reference Library (789 Yonge Street)\, 2nd floor\n
 Time:\nDoors open 6:00pm\, Event starts 7:00pm.\nTickets:\nFree registrati
 on required.\nTicket policy:\nWe oversell these events to ensure that the 
 greatest number of people have an opportunity to attend. Tickets guarantee
 d until 6:45pm or until capacity is reached. Seating first come\, first se
 rved.\nBar:\nBeer/wine available for purchase (debit/credit only).\n***\nT
 his event is part of our signature\nSalon Series\n\, where we host local a
 nd international authors\, artists and thinkers in conversation about thei
 r new books and big ideas.\nIt is also part of our\nIndigenous Heritage se
 ries\n\, generously supported by TD Bank Group\, through the TD Ready Comm
 itment.\n***\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on 
 this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libr
 aries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only 
 be used for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Regi
 strants may be contacted to fill out a brief survey following the program.
  Questions about how the library handles your information can be directed 
 to Answerline staff at answerline@tpl.ca\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street
 \, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, Appel Salon\, Second Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a85b648f564ef0d72c0eb0a
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
