SUMMARY:How to Publish a Book with a University Press: A Scholarly Publish
 ing Seminar
DTSTART:20261020T150000Z
DTEND:20261020T161500Z
DTSTAMP:20260924T191100Z
UID:MEC-417cce83a9373223e4aae3b833114354@events.yorku.ca
RECURRENCE-ID:20261020T150000Z
SEQUENCE:6
CATEGORIES:Faculty of Graduate Studies,Graduate Program in Development Stu
 dies,Graduate Program in Gender, Feminist and Women's Studies,Graduate Pro
 gram in History,Graduate Program in Humanities,Graduate Program in Interdi
 sciplinary Studies,Graduate Program in Science &amp\; Technology Studies,G
 raduate Program in Social &amp\; Political Thought,Graduate Program in Soc
 io-Legal Studies,Graduate Program in Sociology
CLASS:PUBLIC
CREATED:20260924
DESCRIPTION:James MacNevin and Shalini Nanayakkara\, editors at the Univer
 sity of British Columbia Press\, are pleased to present a book publishing 
 workshop on Tuesday\, October 20\, 2026\, @ 11 a.m. at York Lanes room 242
 . The session will consist of a 45-minute presentation followed by a Q&A p
 eriod. Graduate students\, postdoctoral researchers\, and faculty in the s
 ocial sciences and humanities are welcome to attend.\nThe talk will focus 
 on scholarly book publishing and will provide an opportunity to learn abou
 t the process of publishing with a university press in Canada. Topics of d
 iscussion include:\n\nwhat distinguishes university presses from other pub
 lishers\nhow to locate the appropriate publisher for your work\nhow to pre
 pare a compelling proposal\nhow to turn your thesis into a book\nthe peer 
 review process\nsources of funding for scholarly monographs\nwhat to expec
 t of your publisher and what your publisher will expect of you\n\nEvent De
 tails\nDate: Tuesday\, October 20\, 2026\nTime: 11:00 a.m.–12:15 p.m.\nL
 ocation: 242 York Lanes\nPartner: UBC Press\n*Registration is required | 
 RSVP Link\n\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20260929
LOCATION:242 York Lanes
ORGANIZER;CN="Faculty of Graduate Studies":MAILTO:fgsinfo@yorku.ca
PRIORITY:5
TRANSP:OPAQUE
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/scholarly-publishing-seminar/
X-SOURCE:York University
END:VEVENT
