UID:MEC-e98370ec174883f36207c1cc2fb4dce1@events.yorku.ca
RECURRENCE-ID:20261020T160000Z
SEQUENCE:4
CATEGORIES:Advising,Ask a Nurse,Health Education &amp\; Promotion,Student 
 Counselling, Health &amp\; Well-being,Students,Well-being
CLASS:PUBLIC
CREATED:20260918
DESCRIPTION:Consult a healthcare professional\nStudents juggle a lot\, fro
 m academics and work to family and friends. It can be hard to prioritize y
 our own health and well-being at the same time.\nAsk a Nurse is a confide
 ntial service for York students. Speak to Public Health Nurses from Studen
 t Counselling\, Health & Well-being about your health-related questions\, 
 without an appointment. There is a lot of health-related information onlin
 e and it can be difficult to tell what’s reliable. Our goal is to answer
  your questions\, find solutions and connect you to the most helpful resou
 rces. Come see us in-person or get in touch online ( https://students.yor
 ku.ca/health/ask-a-nurse )!\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20260918
LOCATION:Vari Hall Rotunda
PRIORITY:5
TRANSP:OPAQUE
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/ask-a-nurse-drop-by-tabling-session-10-
 687/
X-SOURCE:York University
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events": "https://events.yorku.ca/events/recovery-college-week-3-making-meaningful-connections/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events
SUMMARY:Recovery College: YU & Balance Week 3 | Making meaningful connecti
 ons: Staying present in conversations
DTSTART:20261020T160000Z
DTEND:20261020T170000Z
DTSTAMP:20260901T132400Z
UID:MEC-58836fbe6a74d8fbef6dbce688905c71@events.yorku.ca
RECURRENCE-ID:20261020T160000Z
SEQUENCE:4
CATEGORIES:Athletics &amp\; Recreation,Bethune College,Calumet College,Col
 leges,Divisions and Special Areas,Faculties,Faculty of Health,Faculty of L
 iberal Arts &amp\; Professional Studies,Faculty of Science,Glendon,Health 
 Education &amp\; Promotion,LA&amp\;PS Colleges,LA&amp\;PS Community Hub,LA
 &amp\;PS Founders College,LA&amp\;PS McLaughlin College,LA&amp\;PS New Col
 lege,LA&amp\;PS Vanier College,Learning Commons,Learning Skills Services,S
 tong College,Student Counselling, Health &amp\; Well-being,Students,the At
 kinson Centre for Mature and Part-time Students,The Centre
CLASS:PUBLIC
CREATED:20260901
DESCRIPTION:Building connections can sometimes feel exciting\, awkward or 
 even a little intimidating.\nIn this week’s session of YU & Balance\, we
  will focus on helping students feel more comfortable meeting new people\,
  strengthening the relationships they already have and recognizing what ma
 kes a connection healthy and supportive.\nStudents will explore ways to:\n
 \nManage social anxiety\nBuild confidence in social settings\nThink intent
 ionally about who they can turn to for support.\n\nThis session is part of
  a 6-week Recovery College series. For each session attended\, participant
 s will receive $5 on their YU-card. To receive the gift card\, you must at
 tend the full session (approximately 45–60 minutes). Unfortunately\, we
 ’re not able to provide gift cards for partial attendance. Gift cards wi
 ll be emailed after the session to the same email address used to register
  and join the session.\nSpace is limited\, and registration is offered on 
 a first-come\, first-served basis. If the session is full and you’d like
  to be added to the waitlist\, please email hstacey@yorku.ca ( mailto:hsta
 cey@yorku.ca ). We’ll reach out if a spot becomes available. If you’re
  registered but can no longer attend\, please let us know as soon as you c
 an so we can offer your spot to another student.\nRegister for Making Mean
 ingful Connections ( https://yorku.zoom.us/meeting/register/DZBtVU0XRby7ft
 XNWY6wrQ )\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20261001
LOCATION:Online (Zoom)
PRIORITY:5
TRANSP:OPAQUE
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/recovery-college-week-3-making-meaningf
 ul-connections/
X-SOURCE:York University
END:VEVENT
