SUMMARY:Customer Segmentation: Who Will Pay for Your Product?
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261020T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261020T200000
UID:6a99ba96b88596143287d991@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This program is part of the Toronto Reference Library's\nEntre
 preneur in Residence\n(EIR) service.\nThe fastest way to start a new busin
 ess is to try to sell it to everybody. This session will teach you to narr
 ow down your target group by using geography\, demographics\, and behavior
 al statistics to determine demand. It will also cover how to spot your ear
 ly adopters\, i.e.\, the people who need what you're building most will be
  flexible while you get it right. We'll discover how to narrow down your t
 arget audience\, and how to determine if you were well informed in your de
 cisions.\nThe program includes a short networking component\, providing pa
 rticipants with an opportunity to connect with other entrepreneurs.\nRegis
 tration recommended. Drop-ins welcome until room capacity is reached.\nTo 
 apply for one-on-one consultations with our resident entrepreneur\, Ryan\,
  please fill out the in-take form available at\ntpl.ca/eir\n. We begin acc
 epting in-take forms on September 28\, 2026 until available slots are fill
 ed.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form
  is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act
 \, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used f
 or event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions abo
 ut how the library handles your information can be directed to Answerline 
 staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto 
 ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, Beeton Hall\, Ground Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a99ba96b88596143287d991
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
