X-SOURCE-ID:events
SUMMARY:Centre for Feminist Research Graduate Student Conference: “Assem
 blia”
DTSTART:20261022T040000Z
DTEND:20261023T040000Z
DTSTAMP:20260715T185400Z
UID:MEC-45af559f3798063d200ffcd455f90e5f@events.yorku.ca
RECURRENCE-ID:20261022T040000Z
SEQUENCE:2
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://events.yorku.ca/wp-content/uploads/2026/0
 7/Assemblia.png
CATEGORIES:Faculty of Graduate Studies,Graduate Program in Gender, Feminis
 t and Women's Studies
CLASS:PUBLIC
CREATED:20260715
DESCRIPTION:Date: October 22\, 2026\nTime: 10:00 AM–4:00 PM\nLocation: Y
 ork University\, Keele Campus\nThe Centre for Feminist Research is pleased
  to announce that we are accepting submissions for our upcoming conference
 \, ASSEMBLIA\, taking place on October 22\, 2026.\nThis is the inaugural c
 onference in what we hope will become an annual event organized by graduat
 e students and members of the CFR. It provides an interdisciplinary forum 
 for emerging and independent artists and scholars by bringing together stu
 dio practice\, criticism and theory\, gender studies\, and art history.\nW
 e welcome academic articles\, poetry\, short fiction\, artworks\, and essa
 ys. Any questions can be directed towards the Assemblia Graduate Student L
 eadership Team (Julia and Ame) at CFRfeministfestival@gmail.com\nThe confe
 rence is free and open to graduate students\, independent scholars\, artis
 ts\, and interdisciplinary practitioners. Any questions can be directed to
 wards the Assemblia Graduate Student Leadership Team (Julia and Ame) at CF
 Rfeministfestival@gmail.com\nOur Objective\nAssemblia is organized through
  a collaborative\, non-hierarchical structure grounded in accessibility\, 
 shared decision-making\, and collective accountability.\nAssemblia approac
 hes feminism as a lived practice—often present even when it is not named
 . Across cultures and histories\, feminist resistance has been misrecogniz
 ed as hysteria\, sanctity\, deviance\, or danger. Assemblia brings togethe
 r people interested in attending to the language of feminism as acts of ca
 re\, survival\, and uprising.\n \nClick HERE  ( https://www.yorku.ca/cf
 r/cfr-feminist-festival-call-for-volunteers/ )to apply to be a volunteer.\
 nClick HERE  ( https://www.yorku.ca/cfr/assemblia2026-information-submis
 sion-guidelines/ )to access the Call for Papers\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20260715
LOCATION:519 Kaneff Tower
ORGANIZER;CN="Centre for Feminist Research":MAILTO:cfr-coor@yorku.ca
PRIORITY:5
TRANSP:OPAQUE
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/centre-for-feminist-research-graduate-s
 tudent-conference-assemblia-2/
X-SOURCE:York University
END:VEVENT
