CREATED:20260929
DESCRIPTION:Regenesis@York\, in collaboration with the Office of Sustainab
 ility and Facilities Services\, is bringing tree planting to the Keele Cam
 pus\, with funding support from the City of Toronto. Come out\, dig in\, a
 nd help us grow a greener York!\nJoin the York community for a hands-on tr
 ee planting event. It’s a chance to get outside\, meet new people\, and 
 help make our campus greener and more climate-resilient.\nMeeting location
 : York Blvd and James Gillies Street (east side of the Rob & Cheryl McEwan
  Building) at 11:30 a.m. The planting will take place beside Boynton Woods
 \, across from York Blvd between James Gillies Street and Keele Street.\nW
 hat to bring: Gloves will be provided. Wear weather-appropriate clothing (
 long pants\, long sleeves and sturdy closed-toe footwear are recommended) 
 and bring a reusable water bottle.\nTree planting also takes place on Wedn
 esday\, October 7 at the same time and location.\nSpots are limited. Regis
 ter here ( https://sustainability.apps01.yorku.ca/machform/view.php?id=648
 19 ).\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20260929
ORGANIZER;CN="Office of Sustainability":MAILTO:sustainability@yorku.ca
PRIORITY:5
TRANSP:OPAQUE
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/tree-planting-2/
X-SOURCE:York University
END:VEVENT
