SUMMARY:Common Hour – Tango Concert
DTSTART:20261022T163000Z
DTEND:20261022T173000Z
DTSTAMP:20260923T201100Z
UID:MEC-ac0d7b02669d3fc473a8a11232e89d82@events.yorku.ca
RECURRENCE-ID:20261022T163000Z
SEQUENCE:1
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://events.yorku.ca/wp-content/uploads/2026/
 09/tango.jpg
CATEGORIES:School of the Arts, Media, Performance &amp\; Design
CLASS:PUBLIC
CREATED:20260923
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a free noon-hour concert featuring Solidaridad Tan
 go ( https://solidaridadtango.ca/ )\, an acclaimed ensemble dedicated to c
 elebrating the rich heritage and vibrant energy of tango.\nLed by Sri Lank
 an-Canadian violinist and composer Aparna Halpé\, the group brings togeth
 er world-class international artistry with Belgian bandoneónist Eva Wolff
  and master double bassist Ignacio Varchausky. Don’t miss this midday sh
 owcase of passion\, community\, and extraordinary musical tradition!\nDate
 : Thursday\, October 22\nTime: 12:30 – 1:30 p.m.\nLocation: Tribute Comm
 unities Recital Hall ( https://www.google.ca/maps/place/83+York+Blvd\,+Nor
 th+York\,+ON+M7A+2C5/@43.7728892\,-79.4999096\,560m/data=!3m2!1e3!4b1!4m6!
 3m5!1s0x882b2e24bf73dcab:0xd9125a796619a45!8m2!3d43.7728892!4d-79.4999096!
 16s%2Fg%2F1tvm3d63?entry=ttu&g_ep=EgoyMDI2MDkyMC4wIKXMDSoASAFQAw%3D%3D )\n
 FREE Admission\nEva Wolff\, Bandoneon\nEva Wolff ( https://solidaridadtang
 o.ca/tfts-eva-wolff ) was born in Ghent\, Belgium in 1978. At the age of 1
 5\, she started studying bandoneón at Codarts\, the Rotterdam Conservato
 ry\, under the guidance of Leo Vervelde. She graduated in 2001. In the sam
 e year she won a scholarship granted by the Netherlands\, which permitted 
 her to live and study for one year in Buenos Aires as a student at the Orq
 uesta Escuela de Tango Emilio Balcarce directed by Emilio Balcarce himself
 .\nIgnacio Varchausky\, Double Bass\nBassist Ignacio Varchausk ( https://w
 ww.ignaciovarchausky.com/ )y is the creator and artistic director of the O
 rquesta Escuela de Tango Emilio Balcarce which was founded in 2000 and is 
 funded by the Ministry of Culture of Buenos Aires. For over 25 years\, Var
 chausky has taught and lectured worldwide\, including at the Teatro Colón
  in Buenos Aires\, the Edgar Varese Conservatoire in Gennevilliers\, the S
 ydney Conservatorium of Music\, CODARTS University of the Arts in Rotterda
 m\, University of London Americas Society in New York\, Ibero-American Ins
 titute in Berlin\, and Reed College in Portland.\nAparna Halpé\, Violin\
 , Viola\, Cello\nAparna Halpé ( https://solidaridadtango.ca/tfts-aparna-h
 alpe ) is a Sri Lankan-Canadian tango violinist\, arranger\, and composer\
 , based in Toronto. She holds Licentiates of the Guildhall School of Music
  and the Royal Schools of Music\, UK. In 2021\, Aparna founded the all-wom
 en\, diversity-focused tango ensemble\, Solidaridad Tango\, creating a tan
 go practice grounded in principles of diversity\, equity\, and inclusion t
 hat foregrounds the careers of immigrant women musicians in tango. In 2025
 \, she founded the free community music-making project\, the Toronto Tango
  Community Orchestra\, which invites musicians of all ages and abilities t
 o experience the joy of learning tango while building stronger community r
 elationships. In 2026\, under Aparna’s direction\, the TTCO was invited 
 by RED Por La Identidad Canada to headline the fundraising event for the A
 buelas de Plaza de Mayo which commemorated the victims of Argentina’s 19
 76 coup.\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20260923
LOCATION:Tribute Communities Recital Hall @ Accolade East Building 83 York
  Boulevard\, Toronto
PRIORITY:5
TRANSP:OPAQUE
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/common-hour-tango-concert/
X-SOURCE:York University
END:VEVENT
