SUMMARY:Co-op Information Session
DTSTART:20261022T170000Z
DTEND:20261022T183000Z
DTSTAMP:20261001T202800Z
UID:MEC-ce916a6c3a313e568546f66654ee5ee1@events.yorku.ca
RECURRENCE-ID:20261022T170000Z
SEQUENCE:5
CATEGORIES:Co-op &amp\; Career Centre,Co-op Information Session,Co-op Mand
 atory Sessions (CCC),Information Sessions (CCC)
CLASS:PUBLIC
CREATED:20261001
DESCRIPTION:\nThe York University Co-op Program provides students with opp
 ortunities for paid\, hands-on learning and valuable industry experience. 
 We encourage you to visit the Co-operative Education website to review pro
 gram details and confirm that you meet the academic requirements.\nDuring 
 this session\, you will learn about:\n\nThe co-op advantage\nEligibility r
 equirements\nProgram fees\nThe registration process\nGeneral Q&A with a Co
 -op Coordinator\n\nYork U Co-op Information Session (live webinar)\nLocati
 on: Online – Link:  https://yorku.zoom.us/my/askcoop\nDate: October 22
 \, 2026\nTime: 1:00 p.m. – 2:30 p.m.\nTarget Audience:\nThese sessions a
 re for York University students intending to begin their first co-op work 
 term in Summer 2027. Before registering\, please self-assess your eligibi
 lity for the program ( https://www.yorku.ca/career-ready/work-opportunitie
 s/co-op/eligibility/ ).\nSessions are available in three formats to suppor
 t your schedule and learning preferences:\n\nIn-person\nLive webinar (Zoom
 )\nSelf-paced online modules through the Co-op Preparatory Course (eClass)
 \n\nLive Session vs. Self-Paced Modules: What’s the Difference?\nBased o
 n student feedback\, we now offer flexible options to complete the require
 d sessions. Each format has unique benefits:\n\nLive sessions (in-person o
 r webinar): Opportunity to ask questions and interact directly with a Co-
 op Coordinator.\nSelf-paced eClass modules: Complete the content at a tim
 e that is most convenient for you.\n\nImportant Reminders:\n\nRequired ses
 sions must be completed for your application to be reviewed.\nAlready atte
 nded a mandatory session within the last 12 months? You do not need to att
 end again.\nAlready admitted to Co-op? You are not required to complete th
 e mandatory sessions or re-apply.\n\nIf you have an eligible work term for
  Summer 2027: Log in to the co-op portal and accept the terms and conditio
 ns when prompted.\n\n\n\nWe look forward to your participation!\nRegister 
 Here [icon name=”chevron-right” class=”small pl-2″]\nAccessibility
 \nIf you require accommodations\, please contact askcoop@yorku.ca\, and a
  member of our team will follow up with you.\nCode of Conduct\nBefore atte
 nding\, please review the Code of Rights and Responsibilities from the Y
 ork University Office of Student Community Relations to help ensure a resp
 ectful and positive experience for all participants.\nGuests who exhibit b
 ehaviour that violates this code may be removed from the event. If you exp
 erience behaviour that does not align with these expectations\, please con
 tact our team at askcoop@yorku.ca.\nHaving trouble logging in? \nPlease 
 make sure you’re using your PPY York U login. When you select SSO (Singl
 e Sign-On)\, you should be prompted to sign in with your PPY credentials. 
 If you use a different login\, you may not be able to access the system.\n
 Register here:\n
