BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aa1a88ef9ed2e00384f513b"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_adults
SUMMARY:Ujima Network
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261023T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261023T130000
UID:6aa1a88ef9ed2e00384f513b@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:A free group program that explores mental wellness through a c
 ulturally responsive lens grounded in the Black Model of Health and Wellbe
 ing and the principles of Nguzo Saba. Participants build self-awareness\, 
 learn about the impacts of social determinants of health\, and support one
  another through talk circles and group activities.\nFree registration is 
 required\, speak to library staff for assistance.\nThis program is in coll
 aboration with\nTAIBU Community Health Centre\n.\nInformation Collection N
 otice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto 
 Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, a
 nd 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program registra
 tion\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles yo
 ur information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n
 \, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Albert Campbell\, Small Meeting Room\, 2nd floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aa1a88ef9ed2e00384f513b
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aaa9e6019094f0c6938903c"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_adults
SUMMARY:LSP: Application for Permanent Residence in Canada
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261023T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261023T120000
UID:6aaa9e6019094f0c6938903c@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:During this workshop\, you will be guided through the process 
 of applying for Permanent Residence in Canada\, including completing the 
 required forms and preparing all necessary documents. If you are planning
  to apply for Permanent Residence\, we invite you to join our workshop.\n
 Free Workshop in English and Mandarin.\nIn partnership with Immigration\, 
 Refugees and Citizenship Canada\, CultureLink Settlement & Community Serv
 ices & Toronto Public Library.
LOCATION:Lillian H. Smith
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aaa9e6019094f0c6938903c
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
