X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Stmikes": "https://stmikes.utoronto.ca/event/conference-children-literature-and-the-christian-imagination"}
X-SOURCE-ID:stmikes
X-SOURCE:UofT St. Michael's College
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261023T133000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261024T170000
DTSTAMP:20260930T185404Z
CREATED:20260817T201739Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260930T185404Z
UID:10007552-1792762200-1792861200@stmikes.utoronto.ca
SUMMARY:Conference: Children\, Literature\, and the Christian Imagination
DESCRIPTION:Bringing together an international group of researchers from a range of disciplines and perspectives\, this conference will explore the intersections of children’s literature and the Christian imagination. Participants will investigate historical and contemporary expressions of Christian thought in literature for young audiences\, and reflect on the opportunities and challenges of scholarship in an age shaped by pluralism\, globalization\, and cultural polarization. \n\n\n\nThere is no fee but please register.
URL:https://stmikes.utoronto.ca/event/conference-children-literature-and-the-christian-imagination
LOCATION:Charbonnel Lounge\, Elmsley Hall (81 St. Mary Street)\, 81 St. Mary Street\, Toronto\, Ontario\, M5S 1J4
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6abafedce8cf1c005cafd482"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_adults
SUMMARY:Coding with Python II
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261023T133000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261023T153000
UID:6abafedce8cf1c005cafd482@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Python is an open source programming language that is used for
  creating web applications\, web content\, mathematics and system scriptin
 g. In this course you will learn how python code works and given time to p
 ractice.\nIn this second Python session we will leverage everything we lea
 rned about loops and blocks in part one to create our very own functions. 
 We'll take a look at how to approach function design\, how to allow users 
 to enter data into functions through arguments\, and how to get our functi
 ons to return results. We will also introduce some new data structures whi
 ch\, unlike variables\, can hold more than one piece of data at a time.\nR
 egistration is required.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal inf
 ormation on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the
  Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The informatio
 n will only be used for event and program registration\, delivery and eval
 uation. Questions about how the library handles your information can be di
 rected to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yo
 nge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Fairview\, Digital Innovation Hub\, 3rd Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6abafedce8cf1c005cafd482
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
