DESCRIPTION:FREE for Academy of Fun and Games! \n\n Speed-run creating you
 r first game in the fully open-source game engine Godot!\n\n In this sessi
 on\, you’ll make a working platformer game and get familiar with the mos
 t important features of this powerful creation tool.\n\n \n \n \n \n \n \n
  \n Workshop Schedule : \n \n \n Sunday October 25th\,  10am - 1pm (3 hou
 rs) \n \n \n \n \n \n \n Outcomes : \n \n \n At the end of this workshop y
 ou will have achieved the following goals: \n \n \n- \n Understand the fea
 tures of the Godot game engine \n\n- \n Creating and animating a working p
 layer character \n\n- \n Using a tilemap and tileset for creating a world 
 \n\n- \n How to use collisions \n\n- \n Obstacles and Enemies w. simple AI
  \n\n- \n \n Pickups and achievements \n \n\n \n Please note: Workshops ne
 ed to start on time - any no-shows will be given away to anyone in attenda
 nce. \n \n \n \n \n Want to get notified next time classes are posted?  \
 n\n Join our mailing list!
LOCATION:TTLMakerspace\, 192 Spadina Ave.\, Toronto\, ON
