SUMMARY:4th Monday Book Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261026T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261026T153000
UID:6a3056badcc1022f0039ae25@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Welcome to\nDeer Park's 4th Monday Book Club\n! We meet monthl
 y to discuss a variety of books chosen by our members.\n2026 Schedule:\nJa
 n. 26.\nQuiet\nby Susan Cain\nFeb. 23.\nThe Rosie Project\nby Graeme Simsi
 on\nMar. 23.\nThe Marriage of Opposites\nby Alice Hoffman\nApr. 27.\nThe B
 ook of Eels\nby Patrik Svensson\nMay 25.\nTrust\nby Hernan Diaz\nJun. 22.\
 nReproduction\nby Ian Williams\nJul. 27.\nCrow Lake\nby Mary Lawson\nAug. 
 24.\nUntil August\nby Gabriel Garcia Marquez\nSep. 28.\nNever Let Me Go\nb
 y Kazuo Ishiguro\nOct. 26.\nBook Selection for Monday Book Club 2027\nThis
  meeting will take place in the Main Floor Program Room\nNov. 23.\nBehind 
 the Beautiful Forevers\nby Katherine Boo\n*Dec. 14.\nMaybe You Should Talk
  to Someone\nby Lori Gottlieb\n*October 26th is a change in the usual Prog
 ram Room since Deer Park is acting as a voting poll that day\n*December 14
 th is a change from the usual schedule\, to accommodate the holiday season
 \nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is
  collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, 
 sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for 
 event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about 
 how the library handles your information can be directed to Answerline sta
 ff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON 
 M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Deer Park\, Room 204\, 2nd Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a3056badcc1022f0039ae25
