BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Preschool": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6abc016d295b3b0033ca03a3"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_preschool
SUMMARY:Rabbit and Bear Paws Puppet Show: Treaties
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261028T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261028T120000
UID:6abc016d295b3b0033ca03a3@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This interactive puppet show from Chad Solomon features charac
 ters from the Rabbit and Bear Paws children's graphic novel series. In thi
 s performance\, audiences will experience the story about aa time when peo
 ple and animals knew that we should only take enough food and water for ou
 r own personal needs. Discover how Rabbit\, Bear Paws and the Animals come
  to this agreement\, to save the food and water for tomorrow. With ONE bow
 l ONE spoon and a whole lot of POPCORN.\nChad Solomon\nis a member of the 
 Henvey Inlet\, First Nation. His grandfather taught him that no matter how
  old you become\, you should always be young-at-heart and that laughter is
  the greatest medicine. This is the spirit behind the comical Adventures o
 f Rabbit and Bear Paws series.\nDrop-in only. No Registration Required.
LOCATION:Spadina Road
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6abc016d295b3b0033ca03a3
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Preschool
END:VEVENT
