SUMMARY:Artist in the Library: Weaving
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261028T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261028T200000
UID:6aa0693aaafa610029625fcb@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:October      7:\nThis workshop will teach participants how to 
 build and thread a      hand loom and begin the process of creating woven 
 textiles.\nOctober      14:\nThis workshop will guide participants through
  some beginner      weaving techniques and we’ll begin ideating around o
 ur woven patches for      the community tapestry.\nOctober      21:\nThis 
 workshop is a self-led weaving session to make space for      participants
  to create their patches for the communal tapestry.\nOctober      28:\nThi
 s workshop is a self-led weaving session to make space for      participan
 ts to finish their patches for the communal tapestry. We’ll also      be
  sewing completed patches to the communal tapestry as they are      comple
 ted.\nRegistration required. W\norkshop materials will be provided for the
  first 15 participants. Feel free to drop-in to sessions if you have the s
 upplies needed. We’ll also reflect on and discuss our connections to we
 aving\, water\, and our communities.\nThis event is part of the\nArtists i
 n the Library\nprogram.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal info
 rmation on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the 
 Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information
  will only be used for event and program registration\, delivery and evalu
 ation. Questions about how the library handles your information can be dir
 ected to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yon
 ge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Albert Campbell\, Digital Innovation Lab\, 2nd Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aa0693aaafa610029625fcb
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
