SUMMARY:2SLGBTQ+ Book Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261028T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261028T200000
UID:69446bd62c65973d001356bb@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us on the last Wednesday of every month for a warm and li
 vely discussion of 2SLGBTQ+ books! This year we will be reading:\nJanuary\
 n: Biography of X - Catherine Lacey\nFebruary\n: Angry Queer Somali Boy - 
 Mohamed Abdulkarim Ali\nMarch\n: Firebugs - Nino Bulling\nApril\n: Rainbow
  Black - Maggie Thrash\nMay\n: Sorrowland - Rivers Solomon\nJune\n: Stag
  Dance - Torrey Peters\nJuly\n: Peaces - Helen Oyeyemi\nAugust\n: Afterpa
 rties: Stories - Anthony Veasna So\nSeptember\n: To the Moon and Back by 
 Eliana Ramage\nOctober\n: The Loves of My Life: A Sex Memoir by Edmund Wh
 ite\nNovember\n: Loveless - Alice Oseman\nPlease note that the book list 
 is subject to change.\nDrop in. No registration required.
LOCATION:Parkdale\, Auditorium
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69446bd62c65973d001356bb
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ab6ce03101eb7003f32ebfe"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_adults
SUMMARY:Funding Your Vision
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261028T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261028T200000
UID:6ab6ce03101eb7003f32ebfe@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This program is part of the York Woods Library’s\nEntreprene
 ur in Residence\n(EIR) service.\nThis workshop maps out the funding pathwa
 ys available to Black entrepreneurs\, including grants\, microloans\, and 
 community lenders. Participants learn what funders look for\, which comes 
 down to readiness\, a clear story\, and credible numbers. A live walkthrou
 gh then demonstrates how to prepare a simple funding application of their 
 own.\nDrop-In\nTo apply for one-on-one consultations with our resident ent
 repreneur\, Leo\, please fill out the in-take form available at\ntpl.ca/ei
 r\n. We begin accepting in-take forms on September 28\, 2026 until availab
 le slots are filled.
LOCATION:York Woods\, Enhanced Learning Centre
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ab6ce03101eb7003f32ebfe
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
