SUMMARY: Lea Bertucci & Norbert Rodenkirchen + Slow Attack Ensemble
DESCRIPTION:Composer Lea Bertucci brings her newest piece for archaic flu
 tes in 8 channels featuring master flautist Norbert Rodenkirchen to the e
 thereal environment at Church of the Holy Trinity. Minimalist ambient act
  Slow Attack Ensemble opens the night.\n\nNorbert Rodenkirchen (of early 
 music ensemble Sequentia) plays a collection of flutes dating from the Re
 naissance to Medieval to Neolithic in Bertucci’s piece “The Days Pass Qui
 ckly Immersed in the Shadow of Eternity”\, filtered through an 8 channel 
 array via Lea’s live electronic sequencing. Lush flutters and chattering 
 notes mingle with drone-like breaths and haunting tones that whistle unde
 rneath it all. Electronic experimenter Chuck Blazevic's Slow Attack Ensem
 ble creates subtle ambient soundscapes that evolve with the soft creeping
  drift of errant fog as digital delay pulls playful tones out of sampled 
 guitar notes. Hypnotic sounds stretch and warble as if on some cosmic con
 veyor belt.\n\nCurated by Tad Michalak.\n\nTickets: showpass https://www.
 showpass.com/lea-bertucci-norbert-rodenkirchen-slow-attack-ensemble/
CATEGORIES:Concert,Experimental-Music,The-Music-Gallery,Church-of-the-Hol
 y-Trinity
