BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Stmikes": "https://stmikes.utoronto.ca/event/magnifica-humanitas-choosing-humanity-in-the-ai-revolution"}
X-SOURCE-ID:stmikes
X-SOURCE:UofT St. Michael's College
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261030T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261031T170000
DTSTAMP:20260908T161226Z
CREATED:20260804T155336Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260908T161226Z
UID:10007550-1793354400-1793466000@stmikes.utoronto.ca
SUMMARY:Magnifica Humanitas: Choosing Humanity in the AI Revolution
DESCRIPTION:— A Symposium on Putting Pope Leo’s “AI Encyclical” into Practice \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nOctober 30-31\, 2026 (Fri/Sat)\, 10:30am – 5:00pm \n\n\n\nFather Madden Hall (in Carr Hall\, 100 St. Joseph St) \n\n\n\nFree admission / Lunch included: Register now \n\n\n\nHow do we maintain our humanity and agency in a world that increasingly revolves around AI? \n\n\n\nFrom workplaces to social media feeds\, from breakthroughs in healthcare research to that question you Googled last night\, AI seems to be permeating every aspect of our lives. But as the ways we think\, work\, live\, and act are being rapidly transformed\, how do we protect and nurture those parts of our humanity that matter most—our dignity\, our agency\, our creativity and moral commitments? \n\n\n\nJoin us as we discern our stakes in the current AI revolution through the lens of Magnifica Humanitas\, Pope Leo’s “AI encyclical.” Through two days of panels\, discussions\, and workshops\, we will explore how the Pope uses Catholic social teaching to engage with the structural realities of AI\, and consider our own practical responses to his call to prioritise human dignity over unrestricted AI development. \n\n\n\nBy asking practical questions about AI in light of Magnifica Humanitas\, this symposium will help us engage critically and faithfully with changing technologies in our own lives\, work\, and service to the world. Whether you are new to the conversation and wanting to learn more or are already confronting pressing issues around AI\, we welcome you to join us in this timely dialogue on navigating the emerging AI frontier. \n\n\n\n__________ \n\n\n\nMagnifica Humanitas Online Reading Group \n\n\n\nMonday evenings (7-8pm) from Sep. 14-Oct. 19 \n\n\n\nUPDATE: sign-ups for the reading group have now closed. \n\n\n\nAre you interested in Pope Leo’s “AI encyclical\,” but daunted by the thought of reading it alone? Have you been tempted to ask ChatGPT for a summary? Join us instead for this virtual reading group and explore the encyclical in conversation with others. Over 6 weekly sessions\, Dr. Ren Ito will facilitate discussions of each chapter of Magnifica Humanitas. Participants will build an understanding of the encyclical’s key arguments\, and will learn to engage with current issues of new technology through the lens of Catholic social teaching. \n\n\n\nParticipants will also have the opportunity to present reflections on and takeaways from the encyclical during a session of our October 30-31 Magnifica Humanitas symposium.
URL:https://stmikes.utoronto.ca/event/magnifica-humanitas-choosing-humanity-in-the-ai-revolution
CATEGORIES:Continuing Education
END:VEVENT
