URL:https://tockify.com/torevent/detail/23639/1793489400000
SUMMARY: THE FAMILY CROW: A Murder Mystery
DESCRIPTION:The Family Crow: A Murder Mystery\n\n\nA MURDER murder myster
 y - and the 100th performance of an acclaimed Canadian puppet show\n\n\nI
 nternationally acclaimed puppeteer Adam Francis Proulx returns to Toronto
  this Halloween for the 100th performance of THE FAMILY CROW: A Murder My
 stery at Factory Theatre.\n\n\nA group of crows is called a murder. So wh
 at happens when there is an actual murder amongst a group of crows?\n\n\n
 You get a MURDER murder mystery!\n\n\nEnter Horatio P. Corvus\, an increa
 singly exasperated detective with one hour\, five crows\, and zero patien
 ce. When a murder is committed within a family of crows\, Horatio must so
 rt through the evidence\, interrogate the suspects and uncover the truth 
 before the killer gets away.\n\n\nPerformed by a singular actor but bring
 ing six characters to life (and death?)\, The Family Crow is a puppet-fue
 lled\, pun-filled theatrical mystery packed with atmosphere\, absurdity a
 nd twists. It's a show for anyone who loves a good story\, a good pun\, a
 nd a good old-fashioned whodunit—with a distinctly avian sense of humour.
 \n\n\nThis special Toronto engagement marks the 100th performance of the 
 show\, making Halloween night an especially appropriate time to return to
  the scene of the crime.\n\n\nCritics have embraced the show's peculiar c
 ombination of puppetry\, comedy and mystery. Liz Nicolls of Edmonton call
 ed it “weird\, cuckoo brilliance” and “a bona fide theatrical caws célèbr
 e\,” while Glenn Sumi of NOW Magazine described it as “delightfully atmos
 pheric.” The Saskatoon StarPhoenix declared that audiences would be “crow
 ing about it to all your friends\,” while CJSF called it “definitely a mu
 st-see.”\n\n\nThe production is directed by Byron Laviolette\, a director
  and dramaturg who has worked with interactive art forms for more than tw
 enty-five years. His work spans clown\, puppetry\, immersive theatre\, au
 dio storytelling and interactive performance. He was the founding Artisti
 c Director of What The Festival\, a founding member of Morro and Jasp\, a
 nd is Resident Director of Pucking Fuppet Co.\n\n\nAbout Adam Francis Pro
 ulx\n\n\nAdam Francis Proulx is a Dora-nominated Canadian theatre artist 
 and one of Canada's most sought-after puppeteers. He is best known for hi
 s solo shows\, including The Family Crow: A Murder Mystery and Baker's Do
 zen: 12 Angry Puppets\, as well as the family musical Emilio's A Million 
 Chameleons\, which recently celebrated an Off-Broadway run.\n\n\nBeyond h
 is own creations\, Proulx has appeared in the first Canadian companies of
  Avenue Q and Disney's Frozen\, and has worked across North America. He p
 erforms as Fuzz the hamster on the Canadian Screen Award-winning The Fabu
 lous Show with Fay & Fluffy on Family Jr.\, where he also writes for the 
 series. In 2025\, he was a Protégé recipient of the Johanna Metcalf Award
 s for the Performing Arts.\n\n\nEvent Details\n\n\nTHE FAMILY CROW: A Mur
 der Mystery\n\nCreated by and featuring Adam Francis Proulx\n\nDirected b
 y Byron Laviolette\n\n\nSaturday\, October 31 · 7:30pm\n\nFactory Theatre
  Mainstage\n\n125 Bathurst Street\, Toronto\n\n\nTickets: $31 Early Bird 
 until October 26 · $40 General Admission\n\nRunning time: 70 minutes · No
  intermission\n\nAge recommendation: 14+\n\nWarnings: Flashing lights and
  loud sounds\n\n\nTickets: www.crowshow.ca http://www.crowshow.ca\n\n
CATEGORIES:Dance---Performance---Theatre,Comedy,Factory-Theatre
