SUMMARY:Growing Native Plants from Seeds
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261103T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261103T190000
UID:6ac7df8829c3d600332e992a@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Growing native plants from seed is an inexpensive and easy way
  to add plants to your garden – but you need to start early! Many native
  plants require several months of cold temperatures to sprout in the sprin
 g.\nJoin this session with Toronto Master Gardeners to learn where to get 
 your seed and how to sow it over the winter for germination in the spring.
 \nAt the end of the program\, native seeds will be given out to attendees\
 , while supplies last.\nSuitable for gardeners of any skill level\, with a
 ny kind of outdoor space.\nDrop-in. No registration required.
LOCATION:Rexdale - Closed
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ac7df8829c3d600332e992a
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
