SUMMARY:Networking: Anywhere\, Anytime with Anyone (Part 1)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261103T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261103T200000
UID:6aaad603ab7a8e0037c241bb@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This program is part of Fort York Library's\nEntrepreneur in R
 esidence\n(EIR) service.\nWhy is the #1 skill that will help you thrive as
  a newcomer entrepreneur networking? This workshop with Entrepreneur in Re
 sidence (Newcomer Focus)\, Jean Chow\, will show you how to build your ne
 tworking skills and help you achieve your professional and personal goals.
  Learn the true meaning of networking and why it’s not what you know and
  it’s not who you know.\nIn this session:\nGet outside your comfort zone
  and grow your confidence in meeting new people.\nEmploy strategies to net
 work effectively both in-person and on-line.\nGain a better understanding 
 of how networking can help you grow your business.\nCome early to network 
 from 6-6:30pm!\nTo apply for one-on-one consultations with our resident en
 trepreneur\, Jean\, please fill out the in-take form available at\ntpl.ca/
 eir\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form
  is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act
 \, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used f
 or event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions abo
 ut how the library handles your information can be directed to Answerline 
 staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto 
 ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Fort York\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aaad603ab7a8e0037c241bb
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a73bd03cca66c2f00a88469"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_adults
SUMMARY:String Secrets:  Violin Scams and Fraud
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261103T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261103T200000
UID:6a73bd03cca66c2f00a88469@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Art crimes have always captured public attention\, but those i
 n the musical world are generally less known.\nJoin us as professional vio
 linist and music historian Susan Spier (MA) gives a presentation on art cr
 imes as related to violins: from simple performance scams\, to counterfeit
  strings\, fake labels\, and instrument fraud.\nAlso covered will be true 
 stories of famous stolen Strads\, exploring the current status of specific
  instruments (if known) and discussing what is being done to prevent such 
 crimes in the future.\nDrop in. No registration required. For more informa
 tion\, please contact the Arts Department at 416-393-7157.
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, Beeton Hall (ground level)
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a73bd03cca66c2f00a88469
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
