SUMMARY:Democracy Fitness: Opinion
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261104T113000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261104T123000
UID:6ab29eda001a4a0e055b2a8f@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Develop and exercise the skills you need to be an active parti
 cipant in everyday democracy in this fun\, interactive\n30-minute\nsession
 .\nDemocracy Fitness expands traditional ideas of what democracy is by exp
 loring the skills that help people participate in civic life\, build conne
 ction\, and work better together.\nIn this session\, we’ll exercise our\
 nOpinion\nMuscle:\nIn a democracy\, you have the right to your own opinion
 s. When we share them with each other\, we discover how they take shape an
 d can be challenged.\nRegistration Recommended. Drop-ins welcome.\nAdults 
 only.\nThis program is offered in partnership with Democracy Fitness Globa
 l and MASS LBP.\nGenerously supported by McConnell Foundation.\nInformatio
 n Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected b
 y the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(
 a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and pr
 ogram registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the libr
 ary handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswe
 rline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, Room 2/3\, 2nd Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ab29eda001a4a0e055b2a8f
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
