X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events": "https://events.yorku.ca/events/recovery-college-yu-balance-week-3-making-meaningful-connections-staying-present-in-conversations/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events
SUMMARY:Recovery College: YU & Balance Week 3 | Making meaningful connecti
 ons: Staying present in conversations
DTSTART:20261104T180000Z
DTEND:20261104T190000Z
DTSTAMP:20260918T185900Z
UID:MEC-7f29f58980570546b1ae814455bdcc31@events.yorku.ca
RECURRENCE-ID:20261104T180000Z
SEQUENCE:3
CATEGORIES:Academic Advising &amp\; Student Success,Advising,Bethune Colle
 ge,Calumet College,Colleges,Faculties,Faculty of Health,Faculty of Liberal
  Arts &amp\; Professional Studies,Faculty of Science,Health Education &amp
 \; Promotion,LA&amp\;PS Colleges,LA&amp\;PS Founders College,LA&amp\;PS Mc
 Laughlin College,LA&amp\;PS New College,LA&amp\;PS Vanier College,Lassonde
  School of Engineering,Learning Commons,Learning Skills Services,Markham C
 ampus,Markham Student Accessibility Services,School of Continuing Studies,
 School of the Arts, Media, Performance &amp\; Design,Stong College,Student
  Accessibility Services,Student Counselling, Health &amp\; Well-being,Stud
 ent Leaders at Markham (SLAM),Student Life,Students,Well-being
CLASS:PUBLIC
CREATED:20260918
DESCRIPTION:This session will be offered in person at York University’s 
 Markham Campus and is open to students from all York University campuses.\
 nBuilding connections can sometimes feel exciting\, awkward or even a litt
 le intimidating.\nIn this week’s session of YU & Balance\, we will focus
  on helping students feel more comfortable meeting new people\, strengthen
 ing the relationships they already have and recognizing what makes a conne
 ction healthy and supportive.\nStudents will explore ways to:\n\nManage so
 cial anxiety\nBuild confidence in social settings\nThink intentionally abo
 ut who they can turn to for support.\n\nThis session is part of a 6-week R
 ecovery College series. For each session attended\, participants will rece
 ive $5 on their YU-card. To receive the gift card\, you must attend the fu
 ll session (approximately 45–60 minutes). Unfortunately\, we’re not ab
 le to provide gift cards for partial attendance. Gift cards will be emaile
 d after the session to the same email address used to register and join th
 e session.\nSpace is limited\, and registration is offered on a first-come
 \, first-served basis. If the session is full and you’d like to be added
  to the waitlist\, please email hstacey@yorku.ca ( mailto:hstacey@yorku.ca
  ). We’ll reach out if a spot becomes available. If you’re registered 
 but can no longer attend\, please let us know as soon as you can so we can
  offer your spot to another student.\nRegister for Making meaningful conne
 ctions: Staying present in conversations ( https://forms.students.yorku.ca
 /view.php?id=499412 )\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20261001
LOCATION:Markham Campus (MK2050)
PRIORITY:5
TRANSP:OPAQUE
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/recovery-college-yu-balance-week-3-maki
 ng-meaningful-connections-staying-present-in-conversations/
X-SOURCE:York University
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Torontobotanicalgarden": "https://torontobotanicalgarden.ca/event/floral-design-program-designing-with-natural-materials-4/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:torontobotanicalgarden
X-SOURCE:Toronto Botanical Garden
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261104T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261125T210000
DTSTAMP:20261010T013517
CREATED:20260617T180728Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260617T180740Z
UID:10001985-1793815200-1795640400@torontobotanicalgarden.ca
SUMMARY:Floral Design Program: Designing with Natural Materials
DESCRIPTION:Learn how to create stunning arrangements using natural materials!\nEach week a different natural material – wood\, branches\, foliage\, and fruit and vegetables – will take centre stage. These elements have always been included in arrangements\, but here we will make them the stars of the show! We will study their forms and shapes\, textures\, sizes\, colouring and characteristics to discover the new and exciting ways they can be used. Join us on this journey of discovery.\n \nCourse fees do not include flowers or supplies. Students are encouraged to find a local flower shop or grocery store to purchase their flowers. A materials list will be e-mailed prior to the start of each class.\n \nPrerequisites: Fundamentals I and Fundamentals II.\n \nLearn more about our Certificate in Floral Design\nWednesdays November 4\, 11\, 18\, & 25\, 6 to 9 p.m.\nPublic $240\, Members $190 (plus applicable taxes and fees).\n \nAbout Margaret Taylor\nFor more than 15 years\, Margaret’s passion for flowers has led her to exhibit\, judge\, demonstrate and teach floral design in Canada and abroad. A recipient of many awards\, Margaret’s accolades include two Canada Blooms’ Founder’s Gold Cups for Best in Show. Margaret has also won Best in Show on three occasions at the provincial triennial show and as a result\, has been chosen to represent Canada in two world shows. It was her greatest honour to exhibit for Canada both in Boston and in India.\n \nMargaret is currently a floral design judge accredited by the Garden Clubs of Ontario\, a horticultural judge accredited by the Royal Botanical Gardens and a rose judge accredited by the Canadian Rose Society. Margaret is also a Sogetsu Ikebana teacher and exhibitor. Much lauded for her design acumen by the horticultural community\, she is a past president of the Garden Club of Toronto and is a coordinator of floral design studies at Toronto Botanical Garden.\n \nJoin Toronto Botanical Garden\nJoin the Toronto Botanical Garden (TBG) as a member to get a discount on this program\, upcoming events and classes\, and free parking. A TBG membership helps you deepen your knowledge and connection to the natural world\, become a part of a dynamic community of plant people\, and be inspired! Become a member!\n \nAdditional Program Information\n\n\n\nPlease review our Refund Policy and Terms of Agreement.\nFor more information on accessibility at the garden please review our Accessibility Features webpage. If you have any accessibility requirements during your program\, please email programsupport@torontobotnicalgarden.ca.\nTo learn more about the Toronto Botanical Garden and our programs\, please review our list of Frequently Asked Questions.
URL:https://torontobotanicalgarden.ca/event/floral-design-program-designing-with-natural-materials-4/
LOCATION:Toronto Botanical Garden\, 777 Lawrence Ave E\, Toronto\, ON\, M3C 1P2\, Canada
