UID:6a8ca2332656cb00467289c7@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:November is Financial Literacy Month.\nPresented by Riverdal
 e Immigrant Women's Centre\, this workshop is an introduction to long-term
  financial planning including retirement savings and better understanding 
 of federal income benefits\, such as\, Canada Pension Plan (CPP) and Old A
 ge Security (OAS). Drop-in program\, first come\, first serve seating.
LOCATION:Mount Dennis\, Lower Level\, Room 2
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a8ca2332656cb00467289c7
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Older Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a78e5d288e9bf280036b754"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_older_adults
SUMMARY:The Recipe Club:  Food for Thought
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261105T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261105T193000
UID:6a78e5d288e9bf280036b754@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Do you enjoy recipes and learning about food. Novice or chef e
 xtraordinaire\, drop in for an evening of culinary adventure.  Each month 
 we will delve into a different topic with lively and friendly  conversatio
 n.  Last year's book club created a 50-page recipe book to take home and 
 enjoy.\nDrop In. No Registration Required.  We meet at 6:30\nSept 10 \; 
 Taking in the harvest:. Storing and keeping our food through the winter\nO
 ct 1:      Thanksgiving  Recipes\nNov  5     Cooking techniques\nD
 ec 3      Holiday Favorites
LOCATION:Taylor Memorial\, meeting room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a78e5d288e9bf280036b754
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
