DESCRIPTION:A hands-on introduction to assistive technology\, including a 
 presentation on the necessity of accessible devices and the ways in which 
 the Organization is involving voices from individuals with disabilities. P
 articipants use real tools to build assistive devices that are later donat
 ed to Canadians with disabilities through the Organization’s community p
 artners. Along the way\, they gain practical experience in science\, techn
 ology\, and engineering while giving back to their community.\n*Participan
 ts receive recognition for community involvement activities (volunteer hou
 rs) applicable to high school graduation requirements. If interested\, ple
 ase bring a relevant community involvement tracking form. *\nAll teens are
