CATEGORIES:Faculty of Graduate Studies,Glendon Masters in Public &amp\; In
 ternational Affairs,Graduate Diploma in Biotechnology,Graduate Diploma in 
 Management,Graduate Diploma in Neuroscience,Graduate Diploma in Profession
 al Accounting,Graduate Program in Administration,Graduate Program in Art H
 istory,Graduate Program in Biology,Graduate Program in Biotechnology Manag
 ement,Graduate Program in Chemistry,Graduate Program in Cinema &amp\; Medi
 a Studies,Graduate Program in Civil Engineering,Graduate Program in Commun
 ication and Culture,Graduate Program in Conference Interpreting,Graduate P
 rogram in Critical Disability Studies,Graduate Program in Dance,Graduate P
 rogram in Design,Graduate Program in Development Studies,Graduate Program 
 in Digital Media,Graduate Program in Disaster &amp\; Emergency Management,
 Graduate Program in Earth &amp\; Space Science,Graduate Program in Economi
 cs,Graduate Program in Education,Graduate Program in Education–Leadershi
 p &amp\; Community Engagement,Graduate Program in Electrical Engineering &
 amp\; Computer Science,Graduate Program in English,Graduate Program in Env
 ironmental Studies,Graduate Program in Film,Graduate Program in Financial 
 Accountability,Graduate Program in French and Francophone Studies,Graduate
  Program in Gender, Feminist and Women's Studies,Graduate Program in Geogr
 aphy,Graduate Program in Global Health,Graduate Program in Health,Graduate
  Program in History,Graduate Program in Human Resources Management,Graduat
 e Program in Humanities,Graduate Program in Information Systems &amp\; Tec
 hnology,Graduate Program in Interdisciplinary Studies,Graduate Program in 
 Kinesiology and Health Science,Graduate Program in Law,Graduate Program in
  Linguistics &amp\; Applied Linguistics,Graduate Program in Management Pra
 ctice,Graduate Program in Mathematics &amp\; Statistics,Graduate Program i
 n Mechanical Engineering,Graduate Program in Music,Graduate Program in Nur
 sing,Graduate Program in Philosophy,Graduate Program in Physics &amp\; Ast
 ronomy,Graduate Program in Political Science,Graduate Program in Political
  Science,Graduate Program in Psychology,Graduate Program in Public Policy,
  Administration and Law,Graduate Program in Science &amp\; Technology Stud
 ies,Graduate Program in Social &amp\; Political Thought,Graduate Program i
 n Social Anthrolology,Graduate Program in Social Work,Graduate Program in 
 Socio-Legal Studies,Graduate Program in Sociology,Graduate Program in Thea
 tre,Graduate Program in Theatre, Dance &amp\; Performance Studies,Graduate
  Program in Translation Studies,Graduate Program in Visual Art,LA&amp\;PS 
 Students-Graduate
CLASS:PUBLIC
CREATED:20260818
DESCRIPTION:Artificial Intelligence is rapidly transforming higher educati
 on\, changing how we teach\, learn\, conduct research\, and support univer
 sity operations. This session will provide an overview of York University
 ’s AI journey\, explore what generative AI is and why it matters\, and e
 xamine the opportunities and challenges AI presents for the higher educati
 on sector\, including environmental considerations and responsible use.\nP
 articipants will learn how to effectively work with AI by combining artifi
 cial intelligence with their own expertise\, discover the AI tools availab
 le and approved at York\, including Microsoft Copilot and GitHub Copilot\,
  explore resources available to graduate students and postdoctoral researc
 hers\, and gain insight into York-developed innovations such as YU AURA an
 d the Modular Authentication & RBAC System (MARS). The session is designed
  to help researchers move beyond AI awareness toward practical\, productiv
 e\, and responsible AI adoption.\nEvent Details\nDATE: Wednesday\, Novembe
 r 11\, 2026\nTIME: 1:00-2:00 p.m.\nLOCATION: Online (Zoom)\n*Registration 
 is required | RSVP Link\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20260818
LOCATION:Live on Zoom @ Zoom
ORGANIZER;CN="Faculty of Graduate Studies":MAILTO:fgsinfo@yorku.ca
PRIORITY:5
TRANSP:OPAQUE
