SUMMARY:Investing Basics
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261112T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261112T150000
UID:69e91f36fca21471b7f0027d@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:THIS PROGRAM IS PRESENTED AT THE HILLCREST LIBRARY.\nNew to in
 vesting? Learn the basics of this important part of financial literacy\, i
 ncluding how to save with\nthe goal of investing\, types of investments\, 
 how to open an account\, types of accounts\, how to avoid financial frauds
  and scams\, and more.\nPresented by the\nCanadian Investment Regulatory O
 rganization\n(CIRO) a national self-regulatory organization that oversees 
 all investment dealers\, mutual fund dealers and trading activity on Canad
 a's debt and equity marketplace.\nRegistration is encouraged\n. Drop-ins w
 elcome until capacity is reached.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe per
 sonal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library 
 under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The i
 nformation will only be used for event and program registration\, delivery
  and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your information 
 can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981
 \, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Hillcrest\, Auditorium
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69e91f36fca21471b7f0027d
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Older Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a8c4fe960ccaf01c02085dd"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_older_adults
SUMMARY:Low Income Retirement Planning
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261112T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261112T160000
UID:6a8c4fe960ccaf01c02085dd@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:November is Financial Literacy Month.\nLearn about government
  benefits\, tax credits\, and strategies to help protect your retirement i
 ncome. Presented by John Stapleton from Open Policy Ontario.\nThese sessio
 ns are designed for seniors with low income and those who advise them.\nRe
 gistration not required. Drop-in welcome.\nThursday Oct 1: What Do Senior
 s Get?\nLearn about benefits for older adults living in Ontario\, includin
 g Canada Pension Plan (CPP)\, Old Age Security (OAS)\, Guaranteed Income S
 upplement (GIS)\, and Guaranteed Annual Income Supplement (GAINS).\nThursd
 ay Oct 15: Understanding the Personal Income Tax System.\nWhat is a taxabl
 e income and how can tax credits\, deductions\, entitlements and exemption
 s help to reduce taxable income.\nThursday Oct 29: Protecting Your Retirem
 ent Income.\nLearn how to reduce claw backs to GIS and GAINS payments if 
 receiving additional income from employment\, a private pension\, or a Reg
 istered Retirement Savings Plan (RRSP).\nThursday Nov 12: Coming to Canada
  and Leaving Canada.\nLearn about eligible benefits for those that reside
 d in Canada for fewer than 40 years between the ages of 18 and 65\, or for
  those planning on emigrating from Canada after retiring.\nThursday Nov 26
 : Tax Credits and Benefits for Seniors and People with Disabilities.\nLear
 n about other tax credits and benefits for seniors\, people with disabilit
 ies\, and caregivers\, including the disability tax credit\, the Canada ca
 regiver credit\, and the home accessibility tax credit.
LOCATION:Queen/Saulter
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a8c4fe960ccaf01c02085dd
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Older Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a11b72b8e677a28001e0617"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_older_adults
SUMMARY:Connecting the Dots(?) Book Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261112T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261112T160000
UID:6a11b72b8e677a28001e0617@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Have you ever wondered why people believe in conspiracies?\nIn
  this book club\, we will be reading books that explore the social conditi
 ons that make people prone to extreme belief.\nThurs. Jun. 11\, 2:00-4:00p
 m\nEscaping the Rabbit Hole by Mick West\nThurs. Jul 9\, 2:00-4:00pm\nBlac
 k Pill by Elle Reeve\nThurs. Aug. 13\, 2:00-4:00pm\nProject Mind Control b
 y John Lisle\n**BOOK CHANGE**\nThurs. Sept. 10\, 2:00-4:00pm\nConspiracy: 
 Peter Thiel\, Hulk Hogan\, Gawker\, and the Anatomy of Intrigue by Ryan Ho
 liday\n**BOOK CHANGE**\nThurs. Oct. 8\, 2:00-4:00pm\nAmerican Alt by Chris
  Lockhart\n**BOOK CHANGE**\nThurs. Nov. 12\, 2:00-4:00pm\nShock Doctrine b
 y Naomi Klein
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, Founder's Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a11b72b8e677a28001e0617
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
