UID:1e43949a1b1cd702dee939d13411dc35@jccc.on.ca
DESCRIPTION:Aki no Tabi — Autumn at the JCCC This fall\, join us at the 
 JCCC for a new seasonal experience celebrating Japanese and Japanese Canad
 ian culture through creativity\, connection\, and hands-on activities. Exp
 lore a variety of workshops and activities\, including: Workshops - Ticket
 s on sale Oct 2\, 2026 at 10am Wagashi Making - Enjoy Daifuku with Atelier
  Wa - SOLD OUT! Ceramics - Autumn Leaves Mamezara with Secret Teatime Croc
 het - Make Your Own Amigurumi with So Craftful Journaling & Paper Craft - 
 Crafting Our Narratives with Erica H. Isomura and Nico Koyanagi Craft acti
 vities Live music Food and drink vendors Local market vendors Inspired by 
 the nostalgic charm of Japan and the cozy feeling of autumn transitioning 
 into winter\, Aki no Tabi is a place to slow down\, create\, connect\, and
  enjoy the season together. Come experience the warmth and nostalgia of au
 tumn at the JCCC. 🍂 Keep an eye on this space for more detailed informa
 tion in the coming weeks!\n\nCategories: Community Event\, Social
LOCATION:Japanese Canadian Cultural Centre
