SUMMARY:Make A Will with the Ontario Bar Association
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261118T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261118T160000
UID:6ac7d85829c3d600332e963a@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:November is Make a Will Month and TPL is delighted to host the
  Ontario Bar Association. Learn about the importance of having a will and 
 powers of attorney for you and your family. Nancy Burton-Vulovic\, a memb
 er of the\nOntario Bar Association\nwho practices Trusts and Estates Law w
 ill speak about the elements of a will\, what happens if you don’t have 
 one\, what are powers of attorney\, why they are important and special con
 siderations to keep in mind when preparing your estate and care plans. Not
 e\, this program is for general information only\, not for drafting indivi
 dual wills.\nDrop-in. No registration required.
LOCATION:Rexdale - Closed
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ac7d85829c3d600332e963a
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
