X-SOURCE-ID:events
SUMMARY:Recovery College: YU & Balance Week 5 | Financial literacy: Unders
 tanding your student financial responsibility
DTSTART:20261118T180000Z
DTEND:20261118T190000Z
DTSTAMP:20260918T190600Z
UID:MEC-e265b71426b39bb25ccf6eca0a578a03@events.yorku.ca
RECURRENCE-ID:20261118T180000Z
SEQUENCE:3
CATEGORIES:Academic Advising &amp\; Student Success,Advising,Bethune Colle
 ge,Calumet College,Colleges,Faculties,Faculty of Education,Faculty of Heal
 th,Faculty of Liberal Arts &amp\; Professional Studies,Faculty of Science,
 Financial Literacy Month,Glendon,Health Education &amp\; Promotion,LA&amp\
 ;PS Colleges,LA&amp\;PS Founders College,LA&amp\;PS McLaughlin College,LA&
 amp\;PS New College,LA&amp\;PS Vanier College,Lassonde School of Engineeri
 ng,Learning Commons,Learning Skills Services,Markham Campus,Markham Studen
 t Accessibility Services,School of Continuing Studies,School of the Arts, 
 Media, Performance &amp\; Design,Stong College,Student Accessibility Servi
 ces,Student Counselling, Health &amp\; Well-being,Student Leaders at Markh
 am (SLAM),Student Life,Students,the Atkinson Centre for Mature and Part-ti
 me Students
CLASS:PUBLIC
CREATED:20260918
DESCRIPTION:This session will be offered in person at York University’s 
 Markham Campus and is open to students from all York University campuses.\
 nTuition\, textbooks\, bus fares\, lunch\, getting a coffee or energy drin
 k to get through your 2nd lecture of the day… expenses add up quickly wh
 en you’re in university.\nIn this week’s session of YU & Balance\, par
 ticipants will:\n\nGet a realistic overview of their financial responsibil
 ities\nLearn how to save money on campus\, build balanced budgets and unde
 rstand the differences between types of student debt.\nStudents will also 
 get a chance to ask Peer Health Educators for advice\, tips and strategize
  on how to be more money conscious.\n\nThis session is part of a 6-week Re
 covery College series. For each session attended\, participants will recei
 ve $5 on their YU-card. To receive the gift card\, you must attend the ful
 l session (approximately 45–60 minutes). Unfortunately\, we’re not abl
 e to provide gift cards for partial attendance. Gift cards will be emailed
  after the session to the same email address used to register and join the
  session.\nSpace is limited\, and registration is offered on a first-come\
 , first-served basis. If the session is full and you’d like to be added 
 to the waitlist\, please email hstacey@yorku.ca ( mailto:hstacey@yorku.ca 
 ). We’ll reach out if a spot becomes available. If you’re registered b
 ut can no longer attend\, please let us know as soon as you can so we can 
 offer your spot to another student.\nRegister for Financial literacy: Unde
 rstanding your student financial responsibility ( https://forms.students.y
 orku.ca/view.php?id=500338 )\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20261001
LOCATION:Markham Campus (MK2050)
PRIORITY:5
TRANSP:OPAQUE
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/recovery-college-yu-balance-week-5-fina
 ncial-literacy-understanding-your-student-financial-responsibility/
