BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ac11e4e9dbc2b002c8c0174"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_adults
SUMMARY:Garden with Purpose: Practical Ecological Gardening
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261125T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261125T150000
UID:6ac11e4e9dbc2b002c8c0174@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:You have the power to create real ecological change — right 
 in your own backyard. In this introductory program\, discover the core pri
 nciples of ecological gardening and learn how to transform your garden int
 o a space that’s both environmentally responsible and visually stunning.
  A Toronto Master Gardener will provide guidance on how to create habitat\
 , manage water wisely\, and reduce your ecological impact — all while cu
 ltivating a landscape rich with beauty and year-round interest. Suitable f
 or gardeners of any skill level\, with any kind of outdoor space.\nThis pr
 ogram is part of TPL's\nOur Fragile Planet\nprogram series\, supported by 
 Friends of Toronto Public Library\, South Chapter.​\nInformation Collect
 ion Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the Tor
 onto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c
 )\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program reg
 istration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handl
 es your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl
 .ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Northern District\, Room 200
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ac11e4e9dbc2b002c8c0174
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6abd4454a85a2c00337c1e0d"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_adults
SUMMARY:CRA Personal Finance
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261125T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261125T153000
UID:6abd4454a85a2c00337c1e0d@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Make the Most of Your Tax Return & Protect Yourself from Finan
 cial Scams\nA representative from the Canada Revenue Agency (CRA) will exp
 lain how filing your taxes can help you access benefits and credits you ma
 y be eligible to receive. The representative will also discuss how to rec
 ognize scams and fraud\, the different methods used by scammers\, how to p
 rotect your personal and financial information\, and what steps to take if
  you believe you have been targeted.  Learn about available programs\, e
 ligibility requirements\, and how to apply. Topics may include:\nCanada Gr
 oceries and Essentials Benefit (CGEB)\nCanada Child Benefit (CCB)\nCanada 
 Workers Benefit (CWB)\nDisability Tax Credit (DTC)\nChild Disability Benef
 it\nCanada Caregiver Credit\nEligibility for benefits and credits\nRegistr
 aion is required.
LOCATION:Richview\, Room A\, 2nd floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6abd4454a85a2c00337c1e0d
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
