DESCRIPTION:Led by TIKA\, the seven session workshop series builds towar
 d the creation of individual vision boards.  Workshops will include: visi
 oning creative futures\, dream mapping\, vision board creation and reflect
 ions. TIKA is a multidisciplinary artist\, composer\, speaker\, and cultur
 al futurist whose work explores healing\, identity\, and collective transf
 ormation. Reflective arts-based experiences creates accessible spaces for 
 imagination and personal growth. Open to all ages 13 plus.\nThis event is 
 part of the\nArtists in the Library\nprogram.\nInformation Collection Noti
 ce:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Pub
 lic Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 
