SUMMARY:The Occult Persuasion and the Anarchist's Solution: From Idea to P
 ublication (Writing Workshop)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261126T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261126T153000
UID:6ac82970f34d34366b3c4f50@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Every book or published work begins with a tiny spark: an idea
 \, an image\, a question\, an experience\, a character\, a voice — or si
 mply the feeling that there's a story impatient to be told. But how do you
  turn that initial spark into an actual book?\nJoin Lisa de Nikolits on he
 r writing journey from idea to publication for her (2019) book\,\nThe Occu
 lt Persuasion and Anarchist's Solution\n. This is a writing workshop for a
 ll levels and for those who are interested in the behind-the-scenes techni
 ques that authors use to generate their stories. Lisa will also read excer
 pts from her book.\nAutographed copies of her books are available to purc
 hase.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this fo
 rm is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries A
 ct\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used
  for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions a
 bout how the library handles your information can be directed to Answerlin
 e staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toront
 o ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, Main Floor\, Beeton Hall Auditorium
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ac82970f34d34366b3c4f50
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
