UID:6ac534b1e06996003a81b5e3@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Are you interested in how to navigate the internet on your per
 sonal devices with improved privacy and understanding the importance of st
 aying safe using social media? If so\, this is the class for you.\nWelcome
  to Digital Privacy 201: Securing your Browser and Privacy Considerations.
 \nIn this program\, you will:\nHow to use public computing environments wi
 th improved privacy\nNavigate the Internet on your personal devices with i
 mproved privacy\nReduce privacy risks through the use of web browser plug-
 ins/extensions\nUnderstand the privacy considerations of using social medi
 a\nPre-Requisites\n: Some computer experience is\nrequired\n\; the ability
  to navigate app menus\, browsers\, and desktop computing features is desi
 rable.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this f
 orm is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries 
 Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be use
 d for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions 
 about how the library handles your information can be directed to Answerli
 ne staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toron
 to ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, Learning Centre #2
