X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Torontobotanicalgarden": "https://torontobotanicalgarden.ca/event/holiday-succulent-workshop-2/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:torontobotanicalgarden
X-SOURCE:Toronto Botanical Garden
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261128T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261128T110000
DTSTAMP:20261010T013517
CREATED:20260916T142234Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260916T142243Z
UID:10002035-1795860000-1795863600@torontobotanicalgarden.ca
SUMMARY:Holiday Succulent Workshop
DESCRIPTION:Join us this holiday season and create a one-of-a-kind succulent!\nCelebrate the festive season with a delightful holiday-inspired succulent arranging workshop! In this creative and relaxing session\, you’ll design a beautiful succulent arrangement in a charming birch-lined tin planter—perfect for adding a touch of natural elegance to your holiday décor or gifting to someone special.\n \nGuided by a succulent expert\, you’ll learn tips and tricks for arranging succulents with a seasonal flair\, including techniques for layering textures\, balancing colours\, and incorporating winter-inspired accents.\n \nAll materials are provided\, including a birch-lined tin planter\, premium succulents\, specialty soil\, and care instruction cards to ensure your arrangement stays vibrant through the holiday season and beyond.\n \nJoin us for this festive workshop and leave with a stunning centrepiece that captures the warmth and beauty of the holidays!\n \nSaturday\, November 28\, 10 to 11 a.m.\nPublic $55\, TBG Members $50 (plus applicable taxes and fees).\n \nAbout Canadian Succulents\nMolly is the owner and operator of the small business Canadian Succulents. Canadian Succulents creates floral arrangements using entirely succulents and cacti plants. They not only arrange and design all of the creations\, but also grow all the plants that can be found in them as well. They operate out of a greenhouse just northeast of the city\, where they grow over 300 varieties of succulents and cacti. They grow and create these designs for wedding centrepieces and favours\, corporate events and gifting\, and hotel and office greenery.\n \nJoin Toronto Botanical Garden\nJoin the Toronto Botanical Garden (TBG) as a member to get a discount on this program\, upcoming events and classes\, and free parking. A TBG membership helps you deepen your knowledge and connection to the natural world\, become a part of a dynamic community of plant people\, and be inspired! Become a member!\n \nAdditional Program Information\n\n\n\nPlease review our Refund Policy and Terms of Agreement.\nFor more information on accessibility at the garden please review our Accessibility Features webpage. If you have any accessibility requirements during your program please email programsupport@torontobotanicalgarden.ca.\nTo learn more about the Toronto Botanical Garden and our programs\, please review our list of Frequently Asked Questions.
URL:https://torontobotanicalgarden.ca/event/holiday-succulent-workshop-2/
LOCATION:Toronto Botanical Garden\, 777 Lawrence Ave E\, Toronto\, ON\, M3C 1P2\, Canada
CATEGORIES:Art
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://torontobotanicalgarden.ca/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/8d30cf1b4ef3fb5faf8c28a35a4bbb71.jpg
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Torontobotanicalgarden": "https://torontobotanicalgarden.ca/event/pressed-flower-candle-workshop/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:torontobotanicalgarden
X-SOURCE:Toronto Botanical Garden
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261128T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261128T113000
DTSTAMP:20261010T013517
CREATED:20260921T134401Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260921T134410Z
UID:10002038-1795860000-1795865400@torontobotanicalgarden.ca
SUMMARY:Pressed Flower Candle Workshop
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a morning of hands-on pressed flower candle making!\nDiscover the simple\, satisfying craft of flower pressing and transform a plain pillar candle into a one-of-a-kind keepsake. Using warm palette knives to gently melt pressed flowers directly into the wax\, you’ll learn a technique that’s part botanical art\, part patience. Choose from a variety of pressed flowers to design your own arrangement. Beginners welcome.\n \nEach attendee will receive one 6″ white pillar candle\, a full selection of pressed flowers to choose from\, and step-by-step guidance on using heated palette knives safely to melt your design into the wax.\n \nSaturday\, November 28\, 10 to 11:30 a.m.\nPublic $65\, TBG Members $60 (plus applicable taxes and fees).\n \nAbout Epiphanie Belanger\nEpiphanie Belanger is the founder of HobbyHub\, a community-driven platform designed to help people try new hobbies in a relaxed environment. What started as a personal curiosity for creative pursuits quickly turned into a mission to make hobbies more accessible\, social\, and fun for beginners.\n \nThrough curated workshops and experiences\, Epiphanie brings people together to explore hands-on creative skills in a welcoming\, low-pressure environment. Epiphanie is passionate about helping people rediscover play\, slow down\, and connect (both with their creativity and with others) one hobby at a time.\n \nJoin Toronto Botanical Garden\n \nJoin the Toronto Botanical Garden (TBG) as a member to get a discount on this program\, upcoming events and classes\, and free parking. A TBG membership helps you deepen your knowledge and connection to the natural world\, become a part of a dynamic community of plant people\, and be inspired! Become a member!\n \nAdditional Program Information\n\n\n\nPlease review our Refund Policy and Terms of Agreement.\nFor more information on accessibility at the garden please review our Accessibility Features webpage. If you have any accessibility requirements during your program please email programsupport@torontobotanicalgarden.ca.\nTo learn more about the Toronto Botanical Garden and our programs\, please review our list of Frequently Asked Questions.
URL:https://torontobotanicalgarden.ca/event/pressed-flower-candle-workshop/
LOCATION:Toronto Botanical Garden\, 777 Lawrence Ave E\, Toronto\, ON\, M3C 1P2\, Canada
CATEGORIES:Art
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://torontobotanicalgarden.ca/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/7bea8fc848077b183f4d5f5dae3a5f7f.jpg
END:VEVENT
