BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Older Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aac7b4a86d845003116f192"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_older_adults
SUMMARY:Google Docs 2: Formatting
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261129T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261129T153000
UID:6aac7b4a86d845003116f192@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Learn how Google Docs can be a useful free tool when you don't
  have access to Microsoft Word. In this follow-up class to Part 1\, use mo
 re formatting tools such as bullets\, numbered lists\, text alignment\, ma
 rgins\, page numbers\, and Help. You will also learn how to copy and paste
  text and images from the internet and explore templates for resumes and l
 etters.\nPrerequisites: Basic mouse and keyboard skills are required.\nFor
 mat: Hands-on with demonstrations\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe per
 sonal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library 
 under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The i
 nformation will only be used for event and program registration\, delivery
  and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your information 
 can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981
 \, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Albert Campbell\, Learning Centre\, 2nd Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aac7b4a86d845003116f192
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
