 m in Translation Studies,Graduate Program in Visual Art,LA&amp\;PS Student
 s-Graduate,Markham Campus
CLASS:PUBLIC
CREATED:20260928
DESCRIPTION:The Faculty of Graduate Studies is hosting a session entitled 
 From Research to Real-World Impact: An Introduction to Knowledge Mobilizat
 ion for Graduate Student Scholars. Join us!\nResearch creates knowledge\, 
 but impact happens when knowledge is shared\, understood\, and used. This 
 interactive session introduces graduate students to the fundamentals of Kn
 owledge Mobilization (KMb) and explores how to move research beyond tradit
 ional academic audiences. Topics will include how to identify key audience
 s\, develop effective knowledge-sharing strategies\, build meaningful part
 nerships\, and communicate research in ways that support social\, communit
 y\, policy\, and professional impact. Whether you are just beginning your 
 research journey or preparing for future careers inside or outside academi
 a\, this session will provide practical tools to help amplify the reach an
 d relevance of your work.\nDate: Tuesday December 1\, 2026\nTime: 12:00-1:
 00 p.m. (ET)\nLocation: Virtual Workshop via Zoom Webinar\nRegistration is
  required: Registration Form ( https://yorku.zoom.us/webinar/register/WN_Q
 jJF7v5jQFiV-H6m70-kwg )\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20260928
LOCATION:Online Zoom Webinar @ Online Zoom Webinar
ORGANIZER;CN="Faculty of Graduate Studies":MAILTO:fgsinfo@yorku.ca
PRIORITY:5
TRANSP:OPAQUE
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/fgs-event-research-to-impact-december-1
 /
X-SOURCE:York University
END:VEVENT
