SUMMARY:Intercultural Communication Competency is a Superpower
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261201T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261201T200000
UID:6aaad774ab7a8e0037c241ff@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This program is part of Fort York Library's\nEntrepreneur in R
 esidence\n(EIR) service.\nHow will having “intercultural communication c
 ompetence” help you in your business? As a newcomer\, you have been expo
 sed to different customs\, norms\, values\, and communication styles. Entr
 epreneur in Residence (Newcomer Focus)\, Jean Chow\, teaches you appropri
 ate and effective words\, tones\, body gestures and facial expressions whe
 n you are negotiating with clients\, vendors\, partners\, employees.\nIn t
 his session:\nAdapt your communication in a language that others can under
 stand.\nDisplay more respect\, patience\, and sensitivity to others’ fee
 lings and needs.\nLearn how managing multicultural teams makes you a more 
 effective leader.\nCome early to network from 6-6:30pm!\nTo apply for one-
 on-one consultations with our resident entrepreneur\, Jean\, please fill o
 ut the in-take form available at\ntpl.ca/eir\n.\nInformation Collection No
 tice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto P
 ublic Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, an
 d 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program registrat
 ion\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles you
 r information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\
 , 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Fort York\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aaad774ab7a8e0037c241ff
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
