BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a5e99f388e9bf2800322b63"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_adults
SUMMARY:Wellness Recovery Action Plan (WRAP)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261205T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261205T130000
UID:6a5e99f388e9bf2800322b63@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:WRAP is for\nanyone\nlooking to strengthen their well-being—
 whether you’re supporting your mental health\, managing stress\, or simp
 ly wanting to feel more balanced and resilient in daily life. Participant
 s will receive a\nWRAP certificate\nupon program completion.\nIn an 8-wee
 k WRAP group\, individuals explore:\nself-care tools like peer connections
 \, relaxation and mindfulness techniques\, stress reduction strategies\, a
 nd more\nresources for keeping well and feeling better in difficult times.
 \nInterested in learning more? Drop in for the information session on\nSat
 urday\, October 17\, 2026\, 10 am-12 pm\n.\nThis WRAP Group meets\nevery S
 aturday\,\nonce a week for 8 weeks\, October 24 - December 12\, 2026\, 10
  am-1 pm\n. Registration closes after week 3\, or when full.\nTTC Presto t
 ickets will be provided.\nSnacks and refreshments are provided for all par
 ticipants. Ingredient lists will be available at the program.\nThis progr
 am is in collaboration with\nGerstein Crisis Centre's WRAP initiative\n. G
 erstein Crisis Centre is solely responsible for the protection of \nperson
 al information collected through the program registration \nprocess.
LOCATION:Maria A. Shchuka\, Children's Program Room - Main Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a5e99f388e9bf2800322b63
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Older Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a7b78fb77177f00306214fa"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_older_adults
SUMMARY:Computers for Beginners 3: Use the Internet
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261205T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261205T113000
UID:6a7b78fb77177f00306214fa@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:An introductory class on the Internet for absolute beginners w
 ith little computer experience.\nIn this third session you will:\nUndersta
 nd how to read a web site address\nPractice using web addresses\nSearch fo
 r information using a search engine\nExplore a web site in detail to under
 stand its key components\nUpon completion of this class students will be a
 ble to use the internet at a beginner level and complete simple searches.\
 nPrerequisites: Computer for Beginners 1 & 2 or basic mouse and keyboardin
 g skills\nFormat: Hands-on with demonstrations\nInformation Collection Not
 ice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Pu
 blic Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and
  20(d). The information will only be used for event and program registrati
 on\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your
  information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\,
  416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Malvern\, Computer Learning Centre
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a7b78fb77177f00306214fa
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Older Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a3e94a686636e3d0050d516"}
