BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Philosophy": "https://philosophy.utoronto.ca/event/logic-and-philosophy-of-science-group-gordon-belot-michigan/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:philosophy
X-SOURCE:UofT Philosophy
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261208T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261208T150000
DTSTAMP:20261009T183814Z
CREATED:20260910T180221Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20261009T183814Z
UID:35768-1796731200-1796742000@philosophy.utoronto.ca
SUMMARY:Logic and Philosophy of Science Group (Gordon Belot\, Michigan)
DESCRIPTION:The Logic and Philosophy of Science Research Group is pleased to welcome as its guest speaker Gordon Belot\, the Lawrence Sklar Collegiate Professor of Philosophy at the University of Michigan. Professor Belot’s primary interests are in philosophy of physics\, philosophy of science\, metaphysics\, and epistemology. His most recent book\, Accelerating Expansion: Philosophy and Physics with a Positive Cosmological Constant\, explores some of the philosophical consequences of modern cosmology\, focusing on the significance of the discovery of the accelerating expansion of the universe for our understanding of time\, geometry\, and physics. \nTalk Title\nTBD \nTalk Abstract\nTBD
URL:https://philosophy.utoronto.ca/event/logic-and-philosophy-of-science-group-gordon-belot-michigan/
LOCATION:Jackman Humanities Building\, Room 418\, 170 St. George Street\, Toronto\, Ontario\, M5R 2M8\, Canada
CATEGORIES:Graduate,St. George
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://philosophy.utoronto.ca/wp-content/uploads/Belot-new-resized.png
END:VEVENT
