X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Older Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ac54d2c377296003a4a2212"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_older_adults
SUMMARY:Chess For Life: Seniors Social
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261208T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261208T153000
UID:6ac54d2c377296003a4a2212@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:The\nChess Institute of Canada (CIC)\ninvites you to join our 
 Chess for Life program - a fun and engaging chess program designed for sen
 iors of all skill levels. Chess Institute of Canada (CIC) is an engaging 
 social chess experience for adults and seniors. Learn the game\, build you
 r skills\, challenge your thinking and discover new strategies while conne
 cting with fellow players. Whether you're making your first move or planni
 ng three moves ahead\, there's a place at the board for you!\nWhether you
 ’re a seasoned player or interested in learning the game - enjoy friendl
 y matches\, sharpen your strategy\, and connect with others in a relaxed\,
  supportive environment. Come make your move!\nPut your mind in play!\nReg
 ister for a reminder. Drop-ins are welcome.\nThe program will take place i
 n the Auditorium located in the basement. Elevator on site. If you have an
 y questions\, please call Bendale Branch at 416-396-8910.\nInformation Col
 lection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the
  Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 
 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program
  registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library h
 andles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline
 @tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.\nAccessi
 bility\nLive or automated closed captioning\, sign language interpretation
 \, intervenor services\, or attendant services are available upon request.
  Please submit your request at least 2 weeks in advance to:\ntpl.ca/access
 ibility-events\n.
LOCATION:Bendale\, Auditorium located in the basement.
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ac54d2c377296003a4a2212
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Older Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aad90be65abe8002a7a5c79"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_older_adults
SUMMARY:Fact or Fiction: Identifying and Combatting Misinformation and Di
 sinformation
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261208T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261208T153000
UID:6aad90be65abe8002a7a5c79@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Are you ready to separate fact from fiction in a world filled 
 with misinformation and disinformation? Join us for an interactive and ent
 ertaining program where we'll dive into the fascinating world of misinform
 ation\, exploring its origins\, impact\, and how to combat it effectively.
 \nThis program is perfect for curious minds of all ages who want to arm th
 emselves with the skills needed to navigate the complex landscape of onlin
 e information responsibly and safely.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe
  personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Libr
