BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Older Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a3e8cc6414ef43d00981be8"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_older_adults
SUMMARY:Quilting Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261208T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261208T200000
UID:6a3e8cc6414ef43d00981be8@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:The focus of this program is to make quilts for donation\, usi
 ng fabrics that have been donated to the group for this purpose.\nParticip
 ants meet weekly to share ideas and inspiration while working on quilts. T
 here are no sewing machines at the library so any sewing is done by hand. 
 Most participants also work on quilts using their own sewing machine at ho
 me. Quilts are completed both as individual projects and as group collabor
 ations.\nNew members are welcome\, and will have access to the instruction
 s\, fabrics\, needle and thread required to contribute on-site to the curr
 ent group project.\nRegarding dates: The quilters will not meet when schoo
 l is out. E.g. March break and during the summer (July and August) and dur
 ing December break.
LOCATION:Jones
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a3e8cc6414ef43d00981be8
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Older Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a84c2cffa71a30d92945a78"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_older_adults
SUMMARY:Evening Book Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261208T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261208T193000
UID:6a84c2cffa71a30d92945a78@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join other book lovers in your community and participate in li
 vely discussions of popular books. This book club will meet every First Tu
 esday of the month for a lively discussion in a welcoming\, relaxed settin
 g. New members are always welcome and encouraged to join.\nSeptember 8\n\,
  2026 -\nThe book of Lost Names by Kristin Harmel\nOctober 13\n\, 2026 -\n
 On the Ravine by Vincent Lam\nNovember 10\, 2026 -\nBad Cree by Jessica Jo
 hns\nDecember 8\, 2026 - The Thursday Murder Club by Richard Osman\nCopies
  of the book are available for borrowing at the Port Union Library.\nDrop-
 in\, no registration necessary.
LOCATION:Port Union\, Meeting Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a84c2cffa71a30d92945a78
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
