BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"City of Toronto Festivals & Events": "https://secure.toronto.ca/webapps/feps_edc-ticketing/#events/216644f0-d05b-410f-a0d0-be3b766b93a8"}
X-SOURCE-ID:toronto_festivals
SUMMARY:Held by Anne Michaels - By the Lake Book Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261208T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261208T190000
UID:ca0cd45e6456563647cb1b35a97afd6d@toronto.ca
DESCRIPTION:Held\, by 2024 Scotiabank Giller Prize winner Anne Michaels\, 
 is a luminous\, fragmented novel about love\, memory\, and the reverberati
 ons of war across generations. Beginning on a First World War battlefield\
 , the narrative moves through time and place to explore how desire and gri
 ef endure beyond a single lifetime. Michaels – renowned poet and author 
 of Fugitive Pieces—weaves history and intimacy into a work of haunting b
 eauty. By the Lake Book Club hosts six Tuesday-night events from February 
 to December with top Canadian authors and Humber Polytechnics alumni. Each
  in-person event features readings\, discussions\, Q&A\, book signings and
  ASL interpretation\, while virtual sessions include live subtitles and au
 dio access.
LOCATION:Assembly Hall\, 1 Colonel Samuel Smith Park Dr\, Etobicoke\, ON
URL:https://secure.toronto.ca/webapps/feps_edc-ticketing/#events/216644f0-
 d05b-410f-a0d0-be3b766b93a8
X-SOURCE:City of Toronto Festivals & Events
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a78e91388e9bf280036b78a"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_adults
SUMMARY:The True Crime Club at Taylor Memorial
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261208T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261208T200000
UID:6a78e91388e9bf280036b78a@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This club is for those who enjoy discussing  true crimes from 
 next door to around the world.  Each month we review a case and then we de
 cide which cases we want to look into next month   We investigate the case
 s on our own using a variety of true crime databases\, podcasts\, books et
 c.   We  then meet to discuss the theories and ideas  around the crime wit
 h one another. We are a passionate group and always discuss cases in a res
 pectful manner.  Come and join us on the second Tuesday of the month   for
  an intimate evening of  True Crime.\nSept 8   Bruce McArthur  a serial
  Killer in our city\nOct 13     The Murders of Tim Bosma and   Laura
  Babcock\nNov  10  Why did Kenneth Lee die
LOCATION:Taylor Memorial\, Meeting room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a78e91388e9bf280036b78a
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Older Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a4eaf9a71ef13620051875c"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_older_adults
SUMMARY:Nonfiction Book Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261208T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261208T200000
UID:6a4eaf9a71ef13620051875c@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join a staff-moderated discussion of select nonfiction titles.
  Explore different types of nonfiction\, real-life stories\, biographies/m
 emoirs\, gain new knowledge\, and engage in lively discussions.\nThis mont
 h's featured title is\nLifespan: Why We Age -- and Why We Don't Have to\nb
 y David Sinclair.\nThis program is hosted on\nZoom\n. The Zoom information
  and link will be shared over email.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe 
 personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Libra
 ry under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). Th
 e information will only be used for event and program registration\, deliv
 ery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your informati
 on can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5
 981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.\n[Start with your own unique 
 description of the Book Club and use the 'Title' button to link to the tit
 le being discussed for the month]
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a4eaf9a71ef13620051875c
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
