SUMMARY:Poetry Circle
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261209T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261209T193000
UID:6ab29830129d8e0031f4347b@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us for an evening of poetry writing and discussion in a w
 elcoming and creative environment! Generate new work with guided prompts\,
  share your work when you're ready\, and support your peers by providing c
 onstructive feedback.\nWhile writing techniques may be discussed\, this is
  not a formal creative writing class\, or an English-language learning cla
 ss.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form
  is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act
 \, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used f
 or event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions abo
 ut how the library handles your information can be directed to Answerline 
 staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto 
 ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Barbara Frum\, Located in Room A on the third floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ab29830129d8e0031f4347b
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
