BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/697104d02c65973d00191244"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_adults
SUMMARY:Movie Screening: Home Alone
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261216T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261216T150000
UID:697104d02c65973d00191244@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:When bratty 8-year-old Kevin McCallister (Macaulay Culkin) act
 s out the night before a family trip to Paris\, his mother (Catherine O'Ha
 ra) makes him sleep in the attic. After the McCallisters mistakenly leave 
 for the airport without Kevin\, he awakens to an empty house and assumes h
 is wish to have no family has come true. But his excitement sours when he 
 realizes that two con men (Joe Pesci\, Daniel Stern) plan to rob the McCal
 lister residence\, and that he alone must protect the family home.\nRated 
 PG\n1 Hour 43 Minutes
LOCATION:Cedarbrae - Closed\, FCCR (First-Floor Auditorium)
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/697104d02c65973d00191244
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ac53584901b02002cc07d01"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aaec6b7129d8e0031f38f88"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_adults
SUMMARY:Finding Recovery Through Exercise Skills and Hope (FRESH)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261216T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261216T150000
UID:6aaec6b7129d8e0031f38f88@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This\n program helps people stay active\, make friends\, learn
  new skills\, and \nhave fun. It involves peer-led group activities which 
 can include crafts\, games\,\n walking\, yoga\, and more. Meet new folks\
 , build social connections\, and tell us\n about programs and services you
  would like to see in the neighbourhood!\nFor our upcoming sessions\, we w
 ill be screening the following films in Program Room A:\nOctober 7:\nSingi
 n' in the Rain\nOctober 14:\nCoco\nOctober 21:\nThe Social Network\nOctobe
 r 28:\nThe King's Speech\nNovember 4:\nEternal Sunshine of the Spotless Mi
 nd\nNovember 11:\nLady Bird\nNovember 18:\nJuno\nNovember 25:\nThe Breakfa
 st Club\nDecember 2:\nMy Cousin Vinny\nDecember 9:\nSecondhand Lions\nDece
 mber 16:\nBlack Swan\nDecember 23:\nScrooged\nDecember 30:\nThe Pursuit of
  Happyness\nDrop in. No registration required.\nSnacks and refreshments ar
 e provided for all participants. Ingredient lists will be available at th
 e program.\nThis program is in collaboration with\nGerstein Crisis Centre'
 s F.R.E.S.H. initiative\n.
LOCATION:Maria A. Shchuka\, Meeting Room A
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aaec6b7129d8e0031f38f88
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
