BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Young Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a9b51cdaafa61002961b2ad"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_young_adults
SUMMARY:How Do AIs "Think"? And Why They Get Things Wrong
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261217T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261217T160000
UID:6a9b51cdaafa61002961b2ad@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:How does a machine actually "think"? Explore the history and l
 atest developments of machine learning.\nIn this class led by our Innovato
 r-in-Residence\,\nRyan Kelln\n\, we'll dig into what's really going on ins
 ide AI systems: how they decide what matters in your question\, where thei
 r training data comes from (and who's missing from it)\, and how hidden in
 structions can sneak into content and hijack an AI. Develop an intuitive u
 nderstanding of how AIs "think" without the math. We'll talk about how AIs
  remember\, how they don't and how they are both similar and different to 
 humans. And we'll ask the question underneath it all: is there anyone home
  inside the machine?\nRegistration is required and will start November 9\,
  2026 at 12:30 PM.\nNote: Your spot will not be guaranteed after 5 minutes
  of the start of the program.\nAfter this time\, remaining seats will be f
 illed on a first come\, first serve basis until capacity is reached.\nInfo
 rmation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is colle
 cted by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sectio
 ns 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event 
 and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how th
 e library handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\
 nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G
 8.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, 2nd Floor eLearning Lab
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a9b51cdaafa61002961b2ad
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events": "https://events.yorku.ca/events/virtual-drop-in-session-master-of-biotechnology-management-mbm-graduate-diploma-in-biotechnology-gdb-3/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events
SUMMARY:Virtual Drop-In Session: Master of Biotechnology Management (MBM) 
 & Graduate Diploma in Biotechnology (GDB)
DTSTART:20261217T153000Z
DTEND:20261217T160000Z
DTSTAMP:20260721T141200Z
UID:MEC-cd6c652e6f498d4363bff3c4b63bd685@events.yorku.ca__20261217
SEQUENCE:4
CATEGORIES:Faculty of Graduate Studies,Graduate Diploma in Biotechnology,G
 raduate Program in Biotechnology Management
CLASS:PUBLIC
CREATED:20260721
DESCRIPTION:The Master of Biotechnology Management  is a course- and 
 experiential learning-based graduate program designed for students who 
 hold a bachelor of science degree in biology\, biological sciences\, bio
 technology\, life science\, or related discipline\, and have little/no wor
 k experience in biotechnology. It provides practical interdisciplinary tra
 ining in biotechnology and management to enhance student competitiveness
  and employability in the biotechnology sector. Graduates from this prog
 ram are prepared to contribute to the sector in roles that require scient
 ific\, technical\, and management skills and competencies.  \nThe Grad
 uate Diploma in Biotechnology is a graduate certification for students w
 ho hold a bachelor of science degree in biology\, biological sciences\, 
 biotechnology\, life science\, or related discipline\, and have little/no 
 work experience in biotechnology. It provides scientific and technical 
 training in biotechnology to enhance graduate competitiveness and emplo
 yability in the biotechnology sector. Students acquire the skills and c
 ompetencies required to address labour gaps in the biotechnology sector
  and strengthen the Canadian economy. \nDrop by one of our virtual sessio
 ns on Thursdays from 11:30 a.m. to 12:00 p.m. to meet the graduate pr
 ogram director and graduate program administrator who will be able to answ
 er questions about the programs. \nRegister in advance for this meeting:\
 nMeeting Registration – Zoom\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20260930
PRIORITY:5
TRANSP:OPAQUE
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/virtual-drop-in-session-master-of-biote
 chnology-management-mbm-graduate-diploma-in-biotechnology-gdb-3/
X-SOURCE:York University
END:VEVENT
