SUMMARY:Creative Screen Printing: Workshop for Younger Adults
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261219T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261219T150000
UID:6a88ce8e36204e08fbb63854@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Discover and learn about the entire process of photo emulsion 
 screen printing and create your own screen print to take home. Create your
  own silkscreen\, expose your hand drawn art\, and print it onto a tote ba
 g.\nYou can bring in extra things to screenprint or upcycle and DIY some h
 oliday gifts.\nThis is an in-person program for\nYounger Adults (18-35)\n.
   Space is limited.  Register online or call 416-396-3975.\n*Registration 
 opens November 19\, 2026.\nAuditorium\n----\nInformation Collection Notice
 :\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Publi
 c Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20
 (d). The information will only be used for event and program registration\
 , delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your in
 formation can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 41
 6-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:S. Walter Stewart\, Auditorium
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a88ce8e36204e08fbb63854
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
