BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a3c343bc7d3cd580062952e"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_adults
SUMMARY:Access to Housing
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261223T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261223T160000
UID:6a3c343bc7d3cd580062952e@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Are you seeking housing support or have questions about afford
 able housing options? Join us at S. Walter Stewart Library for personalize
 d\, one-on-one assistance with a Housing Services Worker.\nEast York Housi
 ng Help Hub is offering information session on the Rent Geared to Income o
 ptions available in\nMyAccesstoHousingTO\nonline system. Housing staff wil
 l support program participants with hands-on supports and help them comple
 te the registration process.\nFor more information or to register please c
 ontact East York Housing Help Hub at 416 698-9306 or email eyhhc@eyetfrp
 .ca.
LOCATION:S. Walter Stewart
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a3c343bc7d3cd580062952e
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ac53584901b02002cc07d02"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aaec6b7129d8e0031f38f89"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_adults
SUMMARY:Finding Recovery Through Exercise Skills and Hope (FRESH)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261223T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261223T150000
UID:6aaec6b7129d8e0031f38f89@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This\n program helps people stay active\, make friends\, learn
  new skills\, and \nhave fun. It involves peer-led group activities which 
 can include crafts\, games\,\n walking\, yoga\, and more. Meet new folks\
 , build social connections\, and tell us\n about programs and services you
  would like to see in the neighbourhood!\nFor our upcoming sessions\, we w
 ill be screening the following films in Program Room A:\nOctober 7:\nSingi
 n' in the Rain\nOctober 14:\nCoco\nOctober 21:\nThe Social Network\nOctobe
 r 28:\nThe King's Speech\nNovember 4:\nEternal Sunshine of the Spotless Mi
 nd\nNovember 11:\nLady Bird\nNovember 18:\nJuno\nNovember 25:\nThe Breakfa
 st Club\nDecember 2:\nMy Cousin Vinny\nDecember 9:\nSecondhand Lions\nDece
 mber 16:\nBlack Swan\nDecember 23:\nScrooged\nDecember 30:\nThe Pursuit of
  Happyness\nDrop in. No registration required.\nSnacks and refreshments ar
 e provided for all participants. Ingredient lists will be available at th
 e program.\nThis program is in collaboration with\nGerstein Crisis Centre'
 s F.R.E.S.H. initiative\n.
LOCATION:Maria A. Shchuka\, Meeting Room A
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aaec6b7129d8e0031f38f89
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/699f559c2866a5b4883e53bd"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_adults
SUMMARY:Mystery Book Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261223T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261223T140000
UID:699f559c2866a5b4883e53bd@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Do you like mystery books? Join a group of mystery lovers for 
 informal discussions. There is no set book each month\, come share your f
 avourite books and learn about new authors.\nInformation Collection Notice
 :\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Publi
 c Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20
 (d). The information will only be used for event and program registration\
 , delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your in
 formation can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 41
 6-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:City Hall
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/699f559c2866a5b4883e53bd
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
