X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Older Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a8f26201c197d11325afeec"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_older_adults
SUMMARY:Knitting and Crochet Circle
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261223T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261223T153000
UID:6a8f26201c197d11325afeec@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:We've moved to Wednesdays!\nExperienced knitter or new\, bring
  your projects with you. New to knitting or crochet? Don’t worry\, just 
 bring your supplies with you and we can help you get started.  Share tips\
 , share stories\, make new friends.\nDrop In
LOCATION:Elmbrook Park\, Program room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a8f26201c197d11325afeec
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Older Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6abc17ba377296003a48773a"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_older_adults
SUMMARY:Housing Help
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261223T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261223T170000
UID:6abc17ba377296003a48773a@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Drop in and work one-on-one with staff from The Housing Help C
 entre (THHC) to determine your housing needs\, connect you to other govern
 ment services\, and to match you with landlords across the city. THHC work
 s with both individuals and families in the City of Toronto to find and ma
 intain affordable\, safe housing.\nThe Housing Help Centre can be contacte
 d at 416-285-8070 or at shhc.ca.
LOCATION:Albert Campbell\, Front Entrance
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6abc17ba377296003a48773a
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Teens": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a887dddd4b10d003008127a"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_teens
SUMMARY:Classic Tiramisu Workshop for Teens
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261223T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261223T150000
UID:6a887dddd4b10d003008127a@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Learn the basics of how to make the classic Italian dessert\, 
 Tiramisu. Chef Yumiko will provide and explain all the ingredients and tak
 e the participants through a simple step-by-step process of creating a del
 icious ready-to-eat dish.\n*Food allergy notice: Please be aware that ingr
 edients used in this program include dairy\, egg and decaffeinated espress
 o. Certain food ingredients may cause allergic reactions in some people.\n
 This program is for teens ages 13-17. Registration required.
LOCATION:Victoria Village\, Program room\, downstairs.
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a887dddd4b10d003008127a
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
