SUMMARY:Seniors E-Connect: Tech Help
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20270102T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20270102T113000
UID:6ac502d696ec3a003ad8986c@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Seniors E-Connect matches older adults with a teen volunteer t
 o provide tech help\, under the guidance of library staff. Learn the basic
 s of using smartphones\, tablets\, and laptops\nand learn about topics suc
 h as library databases\, various mobile apps\, Microsoft Office and Google
  Suite software. Get one on one support in a welcoming and friendly enviro
 nment.\nRegister online\, by phone or in-branch. Please bring your device(
 s) and any information you might need for the inquiry.\nIf you're a teen b
 etween the ages of 13-17 and would like to learn more about becoming a Sen
 iors E-Connect volunteer\, visit the\nSeniors E-Connect Volunteering page\
 nor contact the branch.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal info
 rmation on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the 
 Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information
  will only be used for event and program registration\, delivery and evalu
 ation. Questions about how the library handles your information can be dir
 ected to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yon
 ge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Woodside Square\, Magazine Lounge Area
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ac502d696ec3a003ad8986c
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
