BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Philosophy": "https://philosophy.utoronto.ca/event/global-philosophy-research-interest-group-talk-jeannie-miller-university-of-toronto/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:philosophy
X-SOURCE:UofT Philosophy
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20270304T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20270304T170000
DTSTAMP:20261009T184243Z
CREATED:20260924T205651Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20261009T184243Z
UID:35916-1804172400-1804179600@philosophy.utoronto.ca
SUMMARY:Global Philosophy Research Interest Group Talk (Jeannie Miller\, University of Toronto)
DESCRIPTION:The Global Philosophy Research Interest Group is delighted to welcome as guest speaker Jeannie Miller\, an associate professor in the Department of Near and Middle Eastern Studies at the University of Toronto. Her book\, The Quibbler: Al-Jahiz’s Equivocations in Kitab al-Hayawan and Beyond is a study of the Arabic writings of al-Jahiz\, a foundational 9th-century author and analyzes al-Jahiz’s literary style and unique voice as a performative demonstration of good thinking\, according to his definition. She is currently working on several interconnected studies of the reception and afterlife of Abbasid texts in premodern Islamicate contexts\, using manuscripts as evidence. How were these texts read before the modernizing movements of the 19th and 20th centuries and the advent of a modern notion of “literature”? \nTitle\nTBA \nAbstract\nTBA
URL:https://philosophy.utoronto.ca/event/global-philosophy-research-interest-group-talk-jeannie-miller-university-of-toronto/
LOCATION:Jackman Humanities Building\, Room 418\, 170 St. George Street\, Toronto\, Ontario\, M5R 2M8\, Canada
CATEGORIES:Graduate,St. George
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://philosophy.utoronto.ca/wp-content/uploads/Jeannie-Miller-cropped.png
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Philosophy": "https://philosophy.utoronto.ca/event/language-epistemology-metaphysics-and-mind-research-interest-group-david-bulles-princeton/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:philosophy
X-SOURCE:UofT Philosophy
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20270305T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20270305T170000
DTSTAMP:20261009T184341Z
CREATED:20261009T160915Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20261009T184341Z
UID:36028-1804258800-1804266000@philosophy.utoronto.ca
SUMMARY:Language\, Epistemology\, Metaphysics\, and Mind Research Interest Group (David Bulles\, Princeton)
DESCRIPTION:The Language\, Epistemology\, Metaphysics\, and Mind Research Interest Group is delighted to welcome as guest speaker David Bulles\, an associated professor in the Department of Philosophy at Princeton. He has broad research interests in metaphysics and epistemology. In metaphysics\, he is interested in questions about time\, consciousness\, the self\, laws of nature\, ontology\, infinity\, modality\, explanation\, and fundamentality. In epistemology\, he is interested in the problem of induction\, principles of indifference\, objective chance\, and self-locating belief. \nTalk Title\nTBD \nTalk Abstract\nTBD
URL:https://philosophy.utoronto.ca/event/language-epistemology-metaphysics-and-mind-research-interest-group-david-bulles-princeton/
LOCATION:Jackman Humanities Building\, Room 418\, 170 St. George Street\, Toronto\, Ontario\, M5R 2M8\, Canada
CATEGORIES:Graduate,St. George
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://philosophy.utoronto.ca/wp-content/uploads/d._builes_hs_2026_-too-high-crop.png
END:VEVENT
